1
00:00:01,635 --> 00:00:04,704
(After a wild day,)

2
00:00:04,705 --> 00:00:07,607
(the morning of Day Ten arrives.)

3
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:14,580
(Malang is already bustling
with morning life.)

4
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:16,783
(Their accommodations in Malang)

5
00:00:16,784 --> 00:00:18,017
Let's go!

6
00:00:19,421 --> 00:00:20,920
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

7
00:00:20,921 --> 00:00:24,424
(The girls are back
to their usual selves!)

8
00:00:24,826 --> 00:00:26,659
Our driver must be here.

9
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:27,827
Good morning!

10
00:00:27,828 --> 00:00:29,161
- Hello.
- Good morning.

11
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:31,898
- Are you our private driver?
- Yes!

12
00:00:33,801 --> 00:00:35,435
- One suitcase.
- Please load it in the trunk.

13
00:00:35,436 --> 00:00:37,203
(Their fifth member gets loaded
into the car first.)

14
00:00:37,304 --> 00:00:39,038
Anyone else want to put their bag
in the trunk?

15
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:41,407
(Tossing their bags into the trunk)

16
00:00:41,843 --> 00:00:43,076
Ready?

17
00:00:44,745 --> 00:00:48,715
(The younger ones grab
the front and back rows.)

18
00:00:48,849 --> 00:00:50,384
(Now the older ones hop in.)

19
00:00:50,385 --> 00:00:51,784
- Yes!
- Nice!

20
00:00:52,352 --> 00:00:53,852
This chartered car is so nice.

21
00:00:54,155 --> 00:00:55,155
Did you book this just for us?

22
00:00:55,156 --> 00:00:56,956
Yesterday, I booked a private car...

23
00:00:56,957 --> 00:00:58,025
for us...

24
00:00:58,026 --> 00:00:59,525
so we could travel in comfort.

25
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,460
- Sweet.
- That's so thoughtful!

26
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:03,896
This'll be a relaxing ride.

27
00:01:05,199 --> 00:01:06,532
Do you feel like a whole new person?

28
00:01:06,533 --> 00:01:08,167
Like I just flew in fresh from Korea.

29
00:01:22,482 --> 00:01:24,217
I was terrified for her.

30
00:01:24,218 --> 00:01:25,718
I genuinely thought my time had come, too.

31
00:01:26,019 --> 00:01:28,354
I wouldn't have panicked
if you were just quiet,

32
00:01:28,355 --> 00:01:29,722
but you're never this quiet!

33
00:01:29,723 --> 00:01:32,658
- She went completely silent.
- I totally shut down.

34
00:01:32,659 --> 00:01:33,993
I was so scared.

35
00:01:33,994 --> 00:01:35,928
I'm feeling way better today, though.

36
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:38,230
- Thank goodness.
- What a relief.

37
00:01:38,564 --> 00:01:41,033
Yesterday,
I was literally clutching my stomach...

38
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:43,603
binge-watching your YouTube videos.

39
00:01:44,004 --> 00:01:46,006
- Me too!
- I was watching yours, too!

40
00:01:46,007 --> 00:01:48,140
I watched yours and Sian's!

41
00:01:48,141 --> 00:01:49,442
Same here!

42
00:01:50,177 --> 00:01:51,945
That's wild. I was watching yours, too.

43
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:53,480
I watch her videos...

44
00:01:55,415 --> 00:01:56,482
I've seen you do that.

45
00:01:56,483 --> 00:01:59,118
To be honest, I just missed you guys.

46
00:01:59,821 --> 00:02:01,788
I got a little separation anxiety...

47
00:02:01,789 --> 00:02:04,190
- Really?
- the second we were apart.

48
00:02:05,259 --> 00:02:07,761
- It felt so lonely without you.
- Same!

49
00:02:07,762 --> 00:02:09,862
Me too! Going to sleep alone
felt kind of eerie.

50
00:02:09,863 --> 00:02:12,899
I finally get how your subscribers feel.

51
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,935
"They find comfort in watching you."

52
00:02:15,936 --> 00:02:17,436
"Your videos really keep them going."

53
00:02:17,437 --> 00:02:18,337
Totally.

54
00:02:18,338 --> 00:02:21,173
We kept each other going.

55
00:02:21,441 --> 00:02:23,342
It's so adorable that we were
all watching each other's videos.

56
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:24,943
(Catching up on last night's drama)

57
00:02:24,944 --> 00:02:27,045
- Buckle up, everyone.
- Got it.

58
00:02:27,381 --> 00:02:30,117
He says it's a three-hour drive from here.

59
00:02:30,118 --> 00:02:30,950
Sounds good.

60
00:02:30,951 --> 00:02:32,652
(Three hours to Tumpak Sewu Waterfall)

61
00:02:32,953 --> 00:02:35,021
There are so many running clubs out here.

62
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:38,758
(They spotted plenty of runners
near their place too.)

63
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:41,727
Sian and I went for a walk around here.

64
00:02:41,795 --> 00:02:42,795
It had such a hip vibe, right?

65
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:44,663
- Totally.
- Lots of young people everywhere.

66
00:02:44,664 --> 00:02:45,965
This neighborhood...

67
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:47,833
really gave me Seongsu-dong vibes.

68
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:48,867
Lots of cute cafes, too.

69
00:02:48,868 --> 00:02:50,736
The weather is gorgeous here.

70
00:02:50,737 --> 00:02:52,605
We barely even broke a sweat yesterday.

71
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:55,541
There are so many universities
around here.

72
00:02:55,542 --> 00:02:56,909
Everyone looks like a college student.

73
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:58,744
It's definitely the spot to be!

74
00:02:58,745 --> 00:03:00,947
- It's a full-on college town!
- It is.

75
00:03:00,948 --> 00:03:02,114
That's so cool.

76
00:03:02,316 --> 00:03:03,850
College towns always have the best energy.

77
00:03:03,851 --> 00:03:05,618
Should we show them
what we picked up yesterday?

78
00:03:05,986 --> 00:03:07,222
- Yes! Let's do it!
- What did you get?

79
00:03:07,223 --> 00:03:09,622
We got you guys something!

80
00:03:10,657 --> 00:03:11,523
Oh, wow!

81
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:12,825
(Touched)

82
00:03:13,093 --> 00:03:16,262
We checked out a gift shop yesterday.

83
00:03:17,198 --> 00:03:19,632
Our mission was to find
something meaningful to us.

84
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,067
We took care of it...

85
00:03:21,068 --> 00:03:22,668
- for the whole group.
- We even...

86
00:03:22,669 --> 00:03:25,005
customized them ourselves!

87
00:03:25,238 --> 00:03:26,305
- Harimu!
- Harimu!

88
00:03:26,306 --> 00:03:27,873
(Cheering)

89
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:29,075
This one's for Gabee!

90
00:03:29,076 --> 00:03:31,043
(Surprised)

91
00:03:31,044 --> 00:03:32,378
You remembered how much I love eggs!

92
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:34,713
- Each one...
- has something personal on it.

93
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:37,516
Since Harimu is the baby of the group,
she gets a baby bottle.

94
00:03:37,517 --> 00:03:39,017
How cute!

95
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:40,686
I thought this one looked just like me.

96
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:42,788
It really does look like you!

97
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:45,892
It even has the curly hair!

98
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:49,195
Sian is obsessed with ice cream,

99
00:03:49,196 --> 00:03:50,596
- Ice cream!
- so we added that for you.

100
00:03:51,131 --> 00:03:53,132
These are coin pouches, guys.

101
00:03:53,133 --> 00:03:54,767
None of us had a wallet on us.

102
00:03:54,768 --> 00:03:55,768
That's so true.

103
00:03:55,769 --> 00:03:57,236
Wait, there's something else inside.

104
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:58,704
- What's this?
- Oh my gosh!

105
00:03:58,705 --> 00:03:59,939
What is this?

106
00:04:00,607 --> 00:04:02,908
Our very first friendship rings!

107
00:04:04,311 --> 00:04:05,611
They're all different colors.

108
00:04:05,812 --> 00:04:06,745
These are so pretty!

109
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:09,782
We picked colors that matched
everyone's vibe.

110
00:04:09,783 --> 00:04:11,717
Really? This is completely my style.

111
00:04:11,718 --> 00:04:13,586
Who picked this out? Great eye!

112
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:16,255
We chose colors to suit each of us.

113
00:04:16,857 --> 00:04:19,158
It's gorgeous. Such a great find.

114
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:21,160
- Isn't it pretty? It's so delicate.
- Love it.

115
00:04:21,161 --> 00:04:24,130
So, our meaningful group item is...

116
00:04:24,398 --> 00:04:25,665
Our matching rings?

117
00:04:25,832 --> 00:04:27,432
Yes! The pouches and the matching rings!

118
00:04:27,968 --> 00:04:29,736
Let's take a photo together
once we get out.

119
00:04:29,737 --> 00:04:30,703
Sounds like a plan!

120
00:04:30,704 --> 00:04:31,671
Awesome!

121
00:04:31,872 --> 00:04:32,905
I love it so much.

122
00:04:32,906 --> 00:04:34,106
(Official four-way couple
status unlocked!)

123
00:04:34,508 --> 00:04:36,375
Have you guys ever been to a waterfall?

124
00:04:36,376 --> 00:04:38,111
Yeah, plenty of times.

125
00:04:38,311 --> 00:04:39,979
I've visited Cheonjiyeon Waterfall.

126
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:43,148
Cheonjiyeon?
I went there on a school field trip.

127
00:04:43,750 --> 00:04:46,151
I'm skimming through some reviews
right now.

128
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,788
Apparently, the water pours down
from every single angle.

129
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:52,291
Yeah, it falls...

130
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:54,026
in a complete circle around you.

131
00:04:54,161 --> 00:04:55,761
This waterfall is unreal.

132
00:04:56,464 --> 00:04:57,763
We're gonna get completely drenched...

133
00:04:57,764 --> 00:05:00,433
since we can get super close to it.

134
00:05:00,901 --> 00:05:02,568
You can actually hike
right beneath the falls.

135
00:05:02,569 --> 00:05:03,603
You can go right behind them.

136
00:05:03,604 --> 00:05:05,304
Wait, is this full-on waterfall trekking?

137
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,606
It looks way more intense than I thought.

138
00:05:06,607 --> 00:05:07,807
(Getting soaked is
pretty much guaranteed.)

139
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:09,909
I thought we were just admiring it
from a viewpoint.

140
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,744
I had no idea...

141
00:05:12,037 --> 00:05:14,238
we'd be right in the splash zone.

142
00:05:14,448 --> 00:05:16,225
- We can merge with nature.
- Probably!

143
00:05:16,917 --> 00:05:19,819
They rent out water shoes there.

144
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:20,653
Awesome!

145
00:05:20,854 --> 00:05:22,087
It's so great that we can just rent them.

146
00:05:22,088 --> 00:05:24,056
- At least we don't have to buy a pair.
- Exactly.

147
00:05:24,057 --> 00:05:25,825
- Super convenient.
- Buying them would just mean...

148
00:05:25,826 --> 00:05:28,126
- extra luggage to lug around.
- more dead weight in our bags.

149
00:05:28,127 --> 00:05:30,495
Our suitcase is in the car,
so we're covered.

150
00:05:30,597 --> 00:05:32,097
- We can just change after.
- True.

151
00:05:32,098 --> 00:05:33,365
A quick change of clothes and we're good.

152
00:05:33,366 --> 00:05:34,600
(Now fully at peace with getting soaked)

153
00:05:34,734 --> 00:05:36,201
By the way, I'm obsessed with waterfalls.

154
00:05:36,202 --> 00:05:38,036
I love how the water
just never stops rushing.

155
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:40,005
That is so your personality.

156
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:42,174
- Never slow down!
- Just keep moving!

157
00:05:42,309 --> 00:05:43,442
(Rushing water)

158
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:44,743
It just keeps pouring.

159
00:05:44,744 --> 00:05:45,611
(Naturally drawn to things that match her)

160
00:05:45,879 --> 00:05:47,847
There's supposed to be lots
of great street food there, too.

161
00:05:47,848 --> 00:05:49,081
(Looking delicious.)

162
00:05:49,082 --> 00:05:50,316
Let's grab a bite there.

163
00:05:50,717 --> 00:05:53,786
We'll check out the waterfall,

164
00:05:53,787 --> 00:05:57,756
grab some food, head up to Cemoro Lawang,

165
00:05:57,757 --> 00:05:59,191
and check into our hotel.

166
00:05:59,425 --> 00:06:01,893
Then volcano trekking tomorrow!

167
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:04,297
That sounds like a blast.

168
00:06:04,298 --> 00:06:06,632
Back into the wild we go!

169
00:06:07,234 --> 00:06:09,536
This whole trip has really
made me realize...

170
00:06:09,537 --> 00:06:11,337
that whatever I was doing before...

171
00:06:11,605 --> 00:06:12,838
wasn't real travel.

172
00:06:13,607 --> 00:06:15,708
I was basically just shopping
in different countries.

173
00:06:15,709 --> 00:06:16,576
(Giggling)

174
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,244
(Cracking up)

175
00:06:18,245 --> 00:06:19,979
I've never been anywhere
remotely close to...

176
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,314
- a place like Tumpak Sewu.
- Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.

177
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:24,684
I've never explored hidden gems like this.

178
00:06:24,685 --> 00:06:26,619
I'm totally with Gabee on this.

179
00:06:27,187 --> 00:06:31,056
If I'd planned an Indonesia trip on my
own, I would've just landed in Jakarta.

180
00:06:31,658 --> 00:06:33,326
Malang wouldn't have even crossed my mind.

181
00:06:35,428 --> 00:06:37,095
I didn't even know this place existed.

182
00:06:38,298 --> 00:06:39,465
I usually stick to big capital cities.

183
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:40,834
- I probably would've just done Bali...
- Exactly.

184
00:06:40,835 --> 00:06:42,401
or Jakarta.

185
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:45,270
I never really got around...

186
00:06:45,472 --> 00:06:47,106
to venturing off the beaten path.

187
00:06:47,107 --> 00:06:48,374
(Reflecting on trips past,)

188
00:06:48,375 --> 00:06:51,977
(they venture deeper
into the countryside.)

189
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,547
The scenery has completely shifted...

190
00:06:54,848 --> 00:06:55,981
as we drove out here.

191
00:06:56,383 --> 00:06:59,418
You're right. It feels like
a completely different world here!

192
00:06:59,853 --> 00:07:02,322
This landscape gives me major...

193
00:07:02,323 --> 00:07:04,190
Bukit Lawang vibes.

194
00:07:05,158 --> 00:07:08,227
Every town ending in "wang" seems
to look like this.

195
00:07:08,228 --> 00:07:09,595
"Ending in wang?"

196
00:07:10,197 --> 00:07:11,063
Oh, please.

197
00:07:11,064 --> 00:07:12,698
(Gen Z humor at its finest)

198
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:15,401
- I miss Ipu.
- Sounds like he's totally your type now.

199
00:07:15,836 --> 00:07:17,037
He was just so incredible at his job.

200
00:07:17,038 --> 00:07:18,267
A true professional.

201
00:07:18,268 --> 00:07:19,438
(The jungle view brings back
fond memories.)

202
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:20,873
(Taking in the scenery)

203
00:07:20,874 --> 00:07:23,209
Feels like we've climbed up pretty high.

204
00:07:24,010 --> 00:07:24,847
(Winding uphill for about 40 minutes)

205
00:07:24,848 --> 00:07:26,645
We just keep climbing...

206
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:28,814
I guess because we're heading up
to the waterfall basin.

207
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:32,718
Ever since we started shooting this,
it feels like all we do is hike uphill.

208
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:34,219
Somewhere higher.

209
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:35,354
(Swimming upstream like a pack of salmon)

210
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:37,222
They advertised
"four distinct landscapes."

211
00:07:37,223 --> 00:07:38,857
Why does every single one
just feel like mountain climbing?

212
00:07:39,726 --> 00:07:41,205
We're basically an alpine club!

213
00:07:43,563 --> 00:07:45,831
Good grief. We're a hiking squad!

214
00:07:46,099 --> 00:07:47,299
Looks like we've arrived.

215
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:48,667
(The sign reads "Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.")

216
00:07:49,069 --> 00:07:51,437
- Thank you!
- Thank you so much!

217
00:07:52,606 --> 00:07:55,140
(Tumpak Sewu Waterfall parking area)

218
00:07:55,442 --> 00:07:56,942
So, where do we go from here?

219
00:07:57,577 --> 00:07:58,944
I heard...

220
00:07:58,945 --> 00:08:01,446
our guide is supposed to meet us
around here.

221
00:08:01,447 --> 00:08:03,549
- Oh, really?
- Hello!

222
00:08:04,251 --> 00:08:05,821
(Today's guide makes an entrance.)

223
00:08:05,822 --> 00:08:07,720
- Nice to meet you!
- Hello!

224
00:08:07,721 --> 00:08:09,288
My name is Alfin.

225
00:08:09,289 --> 00:08:10,256
- Alfin!
- Alfin!

226
00:08:10,257 --> 00:08:11,657
You can call me Fin.

227
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:12,458
- Fin!
- Fin!

228
00:08:12,459 --> 00:08:13,492
- Fin!
- Fin!

229
00:08:13,493 --> 00:08:15,328
(Welcoming him in their way)

230
00:08:15,329 --> 00:08:16,295
And I'll be...

231
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:18,964
I'll be your guide today
at Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.

232
00:08:18,965 --> 00:08:20,199
Sounds great!

233
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,001
By the way, where are you guys from?

234
00:08:22,269 --> 00:08:23,736
- Korea.
- Korea.

235
00:08:23,737 --> 00:08:24,837
Hello!

236
00:08:25,872 --> 00:08:27,840
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

237
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:29,174
What are your names?

238
00:08:29,542 --> 00:08:31,243
- I'm One.
- One!

239
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:32,377
Two.

240
00:08:32,378 --> 00:08:33,212
Three.

241
00:08:33,213 --> 00:08:34,980
- Four.
- One, Two, Three, and Four!

242
00:08:34,981 --> 00:08:37,416
Make it easy for me.

243
00:08:37,417 --> 00:08:39,184
One, Two, Three, and Four.

244
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:42,421
Today we're heading down
to Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.

245
00:08:42,722 --> 00:08:46,258
We're going all the way down
to the base of the falls.

246
00:08:47,327 --> 00:08:48,193
It takes about 20 minutes.

247
00:08:48,428 --> 00:08:49,461
(That's surprisingly quick!)

248
00:08:49,462 --> 00:08:50,295
Not bad at all!

249
00:08:50,296 --> 00:08:52,030
There are about 500 steps...

250
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:53,298
on the way down.

251
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:55,424
- Got it.
- Wait, 500 steps?

252
00:08:55,425 --> 00:08:56,859
- Five hundred steps.
- To go to the bottom.

253
00:08:59,305 --> 00:09:01,506
We've conquered way more stairs than that.

254
00:09:03,109 --> 00:09:05,110
We literally survived the jungle.

255
00:09:05,111 --> 00:09:06,511
Five hundred is a piece of cake.

256
00:09:06,512 --> 00:09:11,216
For safety,
you'll need shoes with solid grip,

257
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:13,218
like these.

258
00:09:13,219 --> 00:09:15,889
So we'll grab some rental shoes first.

259
00:09:15,890 --> 00:09:17,389
- Sounds good!
- Perfect!

260
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:18,390
Great!

261
00:09:18,825 --> 00:09:20,793
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

262
00:09:21,094 --> 00:09:22,227
- Let's do this!
- Let's go!

263
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:23,762
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

264
00:09:24,698 --> 00:09:27,299
The weather is gorgeous,

265
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:28,734
so I'm in such a great mood.

266
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:30,403
It really is beautiful out.

267
00:09:30,404 --> 00:09:32,238
So cool and breezy.

268
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:33,806
(The perfect breeze lifts their spirits.)

269
00:09:34,307 --> 00:09:37,142
Back into the jungle we go.

270
00:09:37,811 --> 00:09:38,811
It really does look like a rainforest.

271
00:09:38,812 --> 00:09:41,847
(The trail to the falls looks
like deep jungle.)

272
00:09:42,282 --> 00:09:45,517
Wait, is that a cow?

273
00:09:45,518 --> 00:09:46,886
That's a goat.

274
00:09:47,153 --> 00:09:48,353
A goat?

275
00:09:48,354 --> 00:09:50,155
- Definitely a goat.
- That's a goat!

276
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:51,656
It's 100 percent a goat.

277
00:09:51,657 --> 00:09:52,457
(Spotting a goat right
at the trail entrance)

278
00:09:54,561 --> 00:09:57,997
Do you guys live in the city back home?

279
00:09:57,998 --> 00:10:01,300
We all live in Seoul.

280
00:10:01,300 --> 00:10:02,834
- Seoul.
- That's right.

281
00:10:02,965 --> 00:10:04,998
You must live around here, right, Fin?

282
00:10:05,611 --> 00:10:07,939
I live nearby.

283
00:10:08,285 --> 00:10:10,704
When did you start doing this?

284
00:10:10,764 --> 00:10:13,945
I've been working here for a year.

285
00:10:14,024 --> 00:10:15,313
- One year?
- Yeah, since...

286
00:10:15,314 --> 00:10:17,944
I've been working here
since graduating high school.

287
00:10:19,444 --> 00:10:22,035
I'm actually 20 years old.

288
00:10:27,182 --> 00:10:29,594
- You're 20?
- You're just a baby!

289
00:10:30,168 --> 00:10:32,168
- A baby guide.
- Baby guide.

290
00:10:32,169 --> 00:10:34,032
(Alfin, a rookie guide at 20)

291
00:10:34,348 --> 00:10:35,300
Amazing.

292
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:38,570
You're the youngest guide I've ever met.

293
00:10:38,802 --> 00:10:40,802
- Am I the youngest?
- By far!

294
00:10:41,372 --> 00:10:44,709
I've never met a guide younger than him.

295
00:10:46,081 --> 00:10:48,780
- This slope is crazy steep.
- Seriously.

296
00:10:48,848 --> 00:10:50,915
I'm inclined to celebrate this incline.

297
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:53,084
You're ridiculous.

298
00:10:53,186 --> 00:10:55,386
There are so many plants here.

299
00:10:55,599 --> 00:10:57,388
- Coconut trees.
- Coconuts!

300
00:10:57,419 --> 00:10:59,279
They have so many coconuts.

301
00:10:59,280 --> 00:11:01,526
- Look at them hanging over there.
- Coconuts!

302
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:03,967
The trees are packed with coconuts.

303
00:11:04,107 --> 00:11:05,997
- There are durian trees, too.
- Durian trees?

304
00:11:06,397 --> 00:11:08,533
Right there!

305
00:11:08,571 --> 00:11:09,667
That's fascinating.

306
00:11:09,697 --> 00:11:11,069
I've never seen a durian tree
in real life.

307
00:11:12,344 --> 00:11:15,607
When people harvest coconuts around here,

308
00:11:15,617 --> 00:11:18,430
- we just climb right up and pick them.
- Just like that?

309
00:11:18,541 --> 00:11:20,864
- Can you do it?
- No way, I'm scared.

310
00:11:20,991 --> 00:11:22,051
I can do it!

311
00:11:22,052 --> 00:11:23,047
- You can?
- Yeah!

312
00:11:23,171 --> 00:11:26,511
All right, you can try it later.

313
00:11:26,512 --> 00:11:28,137
(Riding high on jungle-tested confidence)

314
00:11:28,611 --> 00:11:31,237
I don't think I've ever walked down
a slope this steep.

315
00:11:31,238 --> 00:11:32,423
Seriously.

316
00:11:33,347 --> 00:11:37,095
Wait, do we have to hike back up this way?

317
00:11:37,367 --> 00:11:38,354
Yes.

318
00:11:38,355 --> 00:11:40,665
So this is just the warm-up.

319
00:11:40,994 --> 00:11:44,441
It gets way harder from here.

320
00:11:44,442 --> 00:11:47,138
This is only the beginning.

321
00:11:48,634 --> 00:11:51,009
- I can smell durian, too.
- You're right!

322
00:11:51,167 --> 00:11:53,077
They're selling so many yummy treats.

323
00:11:53,627 --> 00:11:54,761
Look, real durians!

324
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:56,981
(The alley is packed with street snacks.)

325
00:11:57,649 --> 00:11:59,649
They've got mangosteens, too!

326
00:11:59,951 --> 00:12:01,452
Mangoes!

327
00:12:01,453 --> 00:12:04,560
(Durians and even mangosteens)

328
00:12:05,323 --> 00:12:07,125
It feels like a little mountain village.

329
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:10,261
(A quaint village leading to the falls)

330
00:12:10,293 --> 00:12:14,465
Welcome
to the Tumpak Sewu Waterfall overlook.

331
00:12:15,933 --> 00:12:17,640
- Can we see the falls now?
- Yes.

332
00:12:17,641 --> 00:12:19,147
- You can see it right from up there.
- From over there?

333
00:12:19,148 --> 00:12:20,738
- Yes.
- Awesome.

334
00:12:20,947 --> 00:12:22,273
- Let's check it out!
- Let's go.

335
00:12:22,274 --> 00:12:24,309
We reached the falls way faster
than I thought.

336
00:12:24,681 --> 00:12:27,045
Everyone's staring at the waterfall.

337
00:12:28,146 --> 00:12:30,248
So this is the viewpoint!

338
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:32,773
(A rather crowded overlook)

339
00:12:33,093 --> 00:12:33,680
(Startled)

340
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:35,787
I caught a quick glimpse. It's insane!

341
00:12:35,788 --> 00:12:36,988
- You saw it?
- Yeah!

342
00:12:38,153 --> 00:12:39,942
(Marveling)

343
00:12:43,731 --> 00:12:45,730
It's massive.

344
00:12:51,131 --> 00:12:52,370
It's absolutely monumental.

345
00:12:52,578 --> 00:12:53,938
(Nestled deep in a gorge)

346
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:59,675
(Tumpak Sewu, a geological wonder hidden
deep in the gorge)

347
00:12:59,676 --> 00:13:02,371
(In awe)

348
00:13:03,855 --> 00:13:06,851
- How is this even real?
- It's breathtaking.

349
00:13:07,475 --> 00:13:08,786
- Unreal.
- It's almost terrifying.

350
00:13:09,053 --> 00:13:10,054
Incredible.

351
00:13:10,055 --> 00:13:12,290
It's completely overwhelming.

352
00:13:12,350 --> 00:13:14,324
(The waterfall's staggering scale)

353
00:13:14,325 --> 00:13:15,845
- It's huge.
- It is.

354
00:13:17,509 --> 00:13:20,164
Do you remember what this place is called?

355
00:13:20,348 --> 00:13:23,000
- Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.
- Spot on.

356
00:13:23,001 --> 00:13:24,235
Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.

357
00:13:24,274 --> 00:13:25,970
Tumpak means "cliff."

358
00:13:26,034 --> 00:13:27,038
- Cliff?
- Exactly.

359
00:13:27,039 --> 00:13:30,308
Sewu means a thousand in Javanese.

360
00:13:30,615 --> 00:13:31,581
And it means waterfall.

361
00:13:31,582 --> 00:13:33,945
So it literally means "a thousand
waterfalls pouring from a cliff."

362
00:13:35,881 --> 00:13:37,881
A thousand waterfalls...

363
00:13:38,061 --> 00:13:40,318
What a refreshing sight.

364
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:43,287
(A massive, semicircular curtain
of water cascading 120m down)

365
00:13:43,305 --> 00:13:45,990
I've seen photos,
but they don't do it justice at all.

366
00:13:46,885 --> 00:13:49,427
Mother Nature on a whole different level.

367
00:13:51,662 --> 00:13:53,297
Where does all this water even come from?

368
00:13:53,831 --> 00:13:55,233
Seriously, where is it all coming from?

369
00:13:55,491 --> 00:13:56,334
Right?

370
00:13:56,391 --> 00:13:59,404
- If you trace the main stream...
- Okay.

371
00:13:59,771 --> 00:14:01,239
It flows from a river.

372
00:14:02,807 --> 00:14:05,503
And that river originates
from Mount Semeru.

373
00:14:07,378 --> 00:14:10,263
Waterfalls always blow my mind.
Where does it all come from?

374
00:14:10,789 --> 00:14:15,553
It's been rushing nonstop
for thousands of years.

375
00:14:15,647 --> 00:14:18,967
That mist isn't fog, right?
It's all water spray.

376
00:14:19,590 --> 00:14:22,727
Mount Semeru is the tallest peak
on the island of Java.

377
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:24,195
So the water travels from way far out.

378
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:25,730
(Mount Semeru, the source of the river)

379
00:14:25,731 --> 00:14:28,766
- The tallest mountain in Java?
- In Java.

380
00:14:28,767 --> 00:14:30,767
It's the highest peak.

381
00:14:31,372 --> 00:14:32,804
Does this water ever run dry?

382
00:14:33,404 --> 00:14:35,473
Never. Not even during the dry season.

383
00:14:36,307 --> 00:14:38,342
The flow stays constant all year round.

384
00:14:39,110 --> 00:14:41,612
We've seen so many unreal sights
on this trip.

385
00:14:42,327 --> 00:14:43,181
We truly have.

386
00:14:43,915 --> 00:14:45,647
Wait, are we heading
all the way down there?

387
00:14:45,734 --> 00:14:47,351
Yes, we're hiking all the way
down to the base...

388
00:14:48,052 --> 00:14:49,654
right beneath the waterfall.

389
00:14:50,521 --> 00:14:52,521
Look, there are people down there!

390
00:14:52,667 --> 00:14:53,958
This is mesmerizing.

391
00:14:54,492 --> 00:14:56,894
It just makes you space out and stare.

392
00:14:57,221 --> 00:14:59,305
Looks like it's our turn!

393
00:14:59,978 --> 00:15:01,032
- All right.
- Here we go!

394
00:15:01,198 --> 00:15:02,845
Let's grab a group photo together!

395
00:15:02,846 --> 00:15:04,732
- I can take it for you.
- A group shot?

396
00:15:04,798 --> 00:15:05,736
- Yes.
- Awesome!

397
00:15:05,812 --> 00:15:07,939
I'll shoot a reel for you guys.

398
00:15:12,930 --> 00:15:15,246
Let me show you one I made earlier.

399
00:15:15,852 --> 00:15:18,352
(A sample reel directed by Fin himself)

400
00:15:18,353 --> 00:15:19,584
I think he's filming
a whole cinematic reel for us.

401
00:15:21,258 --> 00:15:22,353
Here's the first shot.

402
00:15:23,832 --> 00:15:26,157
I'll capture you like this as you walk.

403
00:15:26,198 --> 00:15:27,992
- Sounds great!
- Love that!

404
00:15:28,018 --> 00:15:30,561
Just walk along that path,
and in a few seconds,

405
00:15:30,778 --> 00:15:32,958
turn around, look at the camera,
and strike a pose!

406
00:15:32,959 --> 00:15:34,098
- Ah, got it.
- Perfect.

407
00:15:34,195 --> 00:15:35,132
He's on another level.

408
00:15:35,133 --> 00:15:37,301
Our Gen Z guide really knows what's up.

409
00:15:37,915 --> 00:15:41,305
One, two, three, go now!

410
00:15:43,474 --> 00:15:45,676
Turn around and pose!

411
00:15:48,119 --> 00:15:49,113
All right.

412
00:15:49,747 --> 00:15:52,386
- We're basically filming a music video.
- This is amazing.

413
00:15:52,387 --> 00:15:54,452
- That came out so good!
- So cute!

414
00:15:55,299 --> 00:15:57,111
(Pleased)

415
00:15:57,688 --> 00:15:59,824
He's ridiculously good behind the camera.

416
00:15:59,891 --> 00:16:01,025
He's got real talent.

417
00:16:01,064 --> 00:16:02,760
- Fin!
- Yes?

418
00:16:02,884 --> 00:16:05,284
- You're a pro at filming videos!
- Naturally!

419
00:16:05,285 --> 00:16:06,297
I love it.

420
00:16:06,298 --> 00:16:07,932
A complete pro.

421
00:16:07,933 --> 00:16:09,834
Peak Gen Z energy.

422
00:16:09,858 --> 00:16:10,785
Totally built different.

423
00:16:10,786 --> 00:16:12,970
Young guides just hit different.

424
00:16:14,505 --> 00:16:16,741
- Here we are.
- Is this the spot?

425
00:16:21,747 --> 00:16:23,671
(Gearing up
with proper footwear for the falls)

426
00:16:23,672 --> 00:16:25,859
These are surprisingly comfy!

427
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,151
- Comfy, right?
- Totally.

428
00:16:27,172 --> 00:16:27,952
How do they feel?

429
00:16:28,252 --> 00:16:29,645
- These feel much sturdier.
- Agreed.

430
00:16:29,939 --> 00:16:31,584
This color is way cuter, too.

431
00:16:31,585 --> 00:16:32,557
Yes. Thank you!

432
00:16:33,457 --> 00:16:34,825
We need to pay for these rentals.

433
00:16:35,393 --> 00:16:36,527
So, 60,000 rupiah?

434
00:16:37,061 --> 00:16:38,996
Yes, it's 60,000 rupiah.

435
00:16:38,997 --> 00:16:40,665
- Should we pull from the group fund?
- Sure.

436
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:41,799
- Okay.
- Hang on a second.

437
00:16:41,935 --> 00:16:44,635
Since I'm feeling a little
under the weather...

438
00:16:44,975 --> 00:16:48,239
- Won Ji has taken over as treasurer.
- Group fund to the rescue!

439
00:16:49,275 --> 00:16:51,154
(Day Ten Group Fund:
Water shoes, 60,000 rupiah)

440
00:16:51,155 --> 00:16:52,510
Thank you!

441
00:16:54,946 --> 00:16:55,859
How are you doing?

442
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:58,349
Doing great, how are you?

443
00:16:58,647 --> 00:16:59,423
I'm fine.

444
00:16:59,424 --> 00:17:01,469
I can't believe I'm seeing you again!

445
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:02,486
Long time no see!

446
00:17:02,487 --> 00:17:03,187
Right?

447
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:05,456
Didn't we go to the same college?

448
00:17:05,975 --> 00:17:06,757
Wait, what?

449
00:17:08,355 --> 00:17:10,948
(Method acting at its finest)

450
00:17:11,262 --> 00:17:13,397
So cute.
They just launched right into role-play.

451
00:17:13,398 --> 00:17:15,418
(Fin, the ultimate Gen Z guide
and improv master)

452
00:17:15,632 --> 00:17:18,202
All right, let's move!

453
00:17:19,076 --> 00:17:19,804
Okay.

454
00:17:19,865 --> 00:17:21,498
So, are you ready for an adventure?

455
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:23,040
- Yes!
- Born ready!

456
00:17:23,106 --> 00:17:25,668
- Let's roll!
- Is that how you say it?

457
00:17:25,669 --> 00:17:26,744
- Let's go!
- Go now!

458
00:17:26,745 --> 00:17:28,613
- Go now!
- Go now!

459
00:17:28,614 --> 00:17:31,238
(Teaching Fin their catchphrase
before setting off)

460
00:17:31,432 --> 00:17:34,685
It's so great that shoe rentals
exist here.

461
00:17:34,986 --> 00:17:36,554
- So glad we didn't have to buy a pair.
- For real.

462
00:17:36,718 --> 00:17:39,223
The stairs start right here.

463
00:17:39,244 --> 00:17:41,125
We're heading down 500 steps.

464
00:17:41,318 --> 00:17:43,398
All right, let's do this! Go now!

465
00:17:43,399 --> 00:17:45,262
(Rolling down 500 steep steps)

466
00:17:45,263 --> 00:17:47,765
- Got it, locked in memory. Go now!
- Go now!

467
00:17:50,093 --> 00:17:51,335
This is unreal.

468
00:17:52,942 --> 00:17:56,942
(Filmed under official authorization
with local safety guides present.)

469
00:17:57,241 --> 00:17:59,543
It feels like we're descending
straight into Jurassic Park.

470
00:18:00,878 --> 00:18:05,349
If they ever build a real Jurassic Park,
I am so there.

471
00:18:05,367 --> 00:18:06,017
Seriously?

472
00:18:06,018 --> 00:18:08,786
No matter how much tickets cost,
I would go in a heartbeat.

473
00:18:08,807 --> 00:18:10,888
Even with living, breathing dinosaurs?

474
00:18:10,889 --> 00:18:13,958
Yes! If Jurassic Park were real, I'd go
even with real dinosaurs roaming around.

475
00:18:13,959 --> 00:18:14,859
Why on earth?

476
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:17,361
It's just the ultimate vibe!
I'm obsessed with the movie.

477
00:18:17,404 --> 00:18:19,497
- The sheer scale is overwhelming.
- Totally.

478
00:18:20,398 --> 00:18:22,566
This place has
that exact prehistoric feel.

479
00:18:22,567 --> 00:18:24,268
- Like a real-life theme park.
- Utterly jaw-dropping.

480
00:18:24,322 --> 00:18:26,137
Velociraptors wouldn't even look
out of place here.

481
00:18:26,229 --> 00:18:28,673
Have you ever gone trekking before?

482
00:18:28,869 --> 00:18:30,742
- Of course!
- Really?

483
00:18:30,909 --> 00:18:32,009
Hands down!

484
00:18:32,116 --> 00:18:34,180
We hiked through... Where was it again?

485
00:18:34,214 --> 00:18:35,927
Bukit Lawang.

486
00:18:35,928 --> 00:18:37,348
- Bukit Lawang!
- That's the one.

487
00:18:37,349 --> 00:18:39,150
We tracked wild orangutans!

488
00:18:40,076 --> 00:18:42,353
- And monkeys, too!
- You saw monkeys, too?

489
00:18:42,653 --> 00:18:44,653
Have you ever been out to Bukit Lawang?

490
00:18:44,789 --> 00:18:45,589
Not yet.

491
00:18:45,590 --> 00:18:46,622
Never?

492
00:18:46,623 --> 00:18:47,925
- You should.
- Yes.

493
00:18:48,893 --> 00:18:51,128
- Maybe one day.
- Definitely!

494
00:18:51,129 --> 00:18:53,148
(Tourists pitching a domestic trip
to their local guide)

495
00:18:53,221 --> 00:18:54,268
Watch your step right here.

496
00:18:54,269 --> 00:18:55,641
- Watch your footing!
- It's super slick.

497
00:18:55,642 --> 00:18:57,034
The terrain looks so wild.

498
00:18:58,281 --> 00:19:00,574
- He says it gets slippery here.
- Copy that.

499
00:19:01,368 --> 00:19:05,743
I love how hiking like this forces you
to stay completely present.

500
00:19:06,111 --> 00:19:07,812
Look at you getting all philosophical!

501
00:19:07,813 --> 00:19:09,013
No, but that's such a great point.

502
00:19:09,351 --> 00:19:11,351
Just focusing on this exact moment.

503
00:19:11,597 --> 00:19:13,135
You literally can't afford
to look past the next step.

504
00:19:13,557 --> 00:19:15,519
- It's legitimately terrifying.
- Indeed.

505
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:18,780
(A cliffside view that demands
absolute focus)

506
00:19:18,893 --> 00:19:20,791
Let's just stay in the moment.

507
00:19:20,792 --> 00:19:23,060
- That's genuinely deep.
- Truly poetic.

508
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:27,426
(The steep staircase hugs
the sheer cliff face.)

509
00:19:27,693 --> 00:19:30,406
Climbing back up this is
going to be brutal.

510
00:19:30,407 --> 00:19:31,374
I know.

511
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:32,803
This trail is ridiculously tight.

512
00:19:32,953 --> 00:19:34,953
It's super narrow. Watch your balance!

513
00:19:34,954 --> 00:19:37,041
(A treacherous trail narrow enough
for only single file)

514
00:19:37,675 --> 00:19:40,478
We're inching along a knife-edge ledge.

515
00:19:41,011 --> 00:19:44,161
Mad respect to whoever carved these stairs
into the rock.

516
00:19:44,982 --> 00:19:47,184
The more we travel,

517
00:19:47,632 --> 00:19:49,887
the more I'm in awe of the people
who built these paths.

518
00:19:50,472 --> 00:19:54,986
Take your time! I'll head down
ahead to shoot.

519
00:19:54,987 --> 00:19:56,712
- Sounds great!
- Thank you!

520
00:19:57,013 --> 00:19:59,430
He said he'll capture us on camera
if we take it slow.

521
00:19:59,953 --> 00:20:02,299
Fin is seriously the sweetest.

522
00:20:02,702 --> 00:20:06,238
So this was where Fin took the video!

523
00:20:06,839 --> 00:20:07,939
Keep coming.

524
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:10,442
One, two, three, smile!

525
00:20:10,443 --> 00:20:11,976
Hello!

526
00:20:11,977 --> 00:20:13,878
(Cheering)

527
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,480
Let's go!

528
00:20:15,481 --> 00:20:17,048
Let's go, let's go!

529
00:20:17,049 --> 00:20:18,483
Go slowly.

530
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:19,717
Take your time!

531
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:22,587
This is crazy steep.

532
00:20:23,089 --> 00:20:24,406
How did anyone even build this?

533
00:20:24,857 --> 00:20:26,691
- Right?
- Seriously, how did they pull this off?

534
00:20:31,831 --> 00:20:32,664
Totally.

535
00:20:33,799 --> 00:20:36,267
You really have to put all your strength
into your legs on the way down.

536
00:20:36,268 --> 00:20:38,369
I think we've walked down
about 200 steps so far.

537
00:20:38,905 --> 00:20:40,905
Guys, we are about halfway there!

538
00:20:41,274 --> 00:20:42,674
Halfway?

539
00:20:42,675 --> 00:20:44,075
- He said we're halfway there!
- Then 250!

540
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,009
Halfway already!

541
00:20:45,611 --> 00:20:47,178
That's awesome!

542
00:20:47,947 --> 00:20:49,948
It's really not so bad, is it?

543
00:20:50,717 --> 00:20:51,683
- Fin!
- Yeah?

544
00:20:51,684 --> 00:20:53,852
- We have a theme song!
- Yes?

545
00:20:53,953 --> 00:20:57,322
- You wrote a song?
- Yeah, we made our own song!

546
00:20:57,323 --> 00:20:58,156
- Really?
- Yeah!

547
00:20:58,157 --> 00:20:59,557
Yes, she made it up right here!

548
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:02,460
Five, six, seven, eight!

549
00:21:02,461 --> 00:21:04,529
<i>- Abra-ca-Empty!</i>
<i>- Abra-ca-Empty!</i>

550
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:06,297
<i>- Abra, abra-ca-Empty!
- Abra, abra-ca-Empty!</i>

551
00:21:06,866 --> 00:21:10,168
(Dancing together)

552
00:21:10,169 --> 00:21:12,037
<i>- Empty, empty, empty
- Empty, empty, empty</i>

553
00:21:12,038 --> 00:21:13,905
<i>- Empty everything out!
- Empty everything out!</i>

554
00:21:13,906 --> 00:21:15,807
<i>- Reduce, reduce, reduce
- Reduce, reduce, reduce</i>

555
00:21:15,808 --> 00:21:18,477
<i>- Reduce everything!
- Reduce everything!</i>

556
00:21:18,478 --> 00:21:20,946
Wow, that was great!

557
00:21:20,947 --> 00:21:22,180
- Really?
- Yes.

558
00:21:22,915 --> 00:21:26,050
Even though it's my first time hearing it,

559
00:21:26,051 --> 00:21:27,719
it honestly makes me say "wow."

560
00:21:27,720 --> 00:21:28,686
- He really likes our song!
- Really?

561
00:21:28,687 --> 00:21:29,654
- Yeah!
- Thank you!

562
00:21:29,989 --> 00:21:33,091
<i>- Abra-ca-Empty, abra-ca-empty!
- Abra-ca-Empty, abra-ca-empty!</i>

563
00:21:33,225 --> 00:21:34,426
Fin is so sweet.

564
00:21:34,427 --> 00:21:35,927
- You're so kind!
- He really is.

565
00:21:35,928 --> 00:21:36,894
- What?
- You're so sweet!

566
00:21:36,895 --> 00:21:38,162
Thank you!

567
00:21:38,531 --> 00:21:39,531
Yeah, thank you!

568
00:21:39,532 --> 00:21:40,565
(Gen Z guide with sweet reactions)

569
00:21:41,467 --> 00:21:43,033
(Beginning to see little waterfalls)

570
00:21:43,034 --> 00:21:44,402
I think we're almost there!

571
00:21:45,438 --> 00:21:47,205
- Oh my gosh!
- A casual encounter with water!

572
00:21:47,873 --> 00:21:49,807
"A casual encounter with water."

573
00:21:49,808 --> 00:21:52,208
But there is some serious foot traffic
up ahead.

574
00:21:52,209 --> 00:21:52,844
That's wild.

575
00:21:53,879 --> 00:21:54,745
Sorry!

576
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:56,480
It's okay, you're fine!

577
00:21:57,016 --> 00:21:59,084
It's kind of scary right here.

578
00:21:59,218 --> 00:22:00,051
Yeah.

579
00:22:00,286 --> 00:22:01,786
This path is so narrow.

580
00:22:01,887 --> 00:22:04,155
- It's narrow and terrifying!
- I literally freeze when people pass by.

581
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:07,525
It feels like the whole thing
might collapse!

582
00:22:07,526 --> 00:22:10,328
Please pass by quickly. I'm terrified!

583
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:12,763
People just keep on coming.

584
00:22:14,033 --> 00:22:15,533
My legs are shaking.

585
00:22:15,534 --> 00:22:16,701
Tremble, tremble.

586
00:22:16,702 --> 00:22:19,304
My knees are already wobbling.

587
00:22:19,905 --> 00:22:22,006
Okay, let's go!

588
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,207
Let's go!

589
00:22:23,208 --> 00:22:25,209
Let's go, let's go!

590
00:22:25,210 --> 00:22:28,312
You got this!

591
00:22:28,814 --> 00:22:30,014
This lady passing by just went...

592
00:22:30,716 --> 00:22:32,817
"Oh, gosh..."

593
00:22:32,818 --> 00:22:34,052
"Oh, my goodness."

594
00:22:34,053 --> 00:22:35,653
That was her expert advice.

595
00:22:36,689 --> 00:22:38,156
I see our future right there.

596
00:22:39,325 --> 00:22:41,593
The incline is completely insane.

597
00:22:41,994 --> 00:22:43,861
It's practically a 90-degree drop.

598
00:22:44,797 --> 00:22:48,767
(Almost 90 degrees)

599
00:22:49,268 --> 00:22:50,568
It's practically vertical!

600
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:53,271
The steps are super slick.

601
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,206
Keep a firm grip on the rail!

602
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,907
My legs are shaking like crazy.

603
00:23:00,613 --> 00:23:03,748
The actual distance isn't bad, but...

604
00:23:03,749 --> 00:23:05,083
it's insanely steep!

605
00:23:05,719 --> 00:23:07,552
We can do this, though!

606
00:23:08,254 --> 00:23:09,588
We've got this!

607
00:23:09,655 --> 00:23:13,891
(Remaining Steps)

608
00:23:14,393 --> 00:23:15,626
(Gasping)

609
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:18,062
Why is everyone soaked?

610
00:23:20,366 --> 00:23:22,767
They're completely drenched!

611
00:23:22,768 --> 00:23:24,636
(People crawling up all drenched)

612
00:23:24,937 --> 00:23:26,774
I'm getting a bad feeling about this.

613
00:23:26,775 --> 00:23:29,674
Seeing them that drenched is giving me
serious anxiety.

614
00:23:31,343 --> 00:23:32,677
Whoa, look at that!

615
00:23:34,146 --> 00:23:35,947
(Screaming)

616
00:23:35,948 --> 00:23:36,848
Come down slowly.

617
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:39,183
This is unreal.

618
00:23:39,184 --> 00:23:40,351
(Next course up)

619
00:23:40,352 --> 00:23:41,185
I can't believe my eyes.

620
00:23:41,987 --> 00:23:44,188
The stairs are
right beside the rushing waterfall!

621
00:23:44,189 --> 00:23:45,656
Look, there's a rope!

622
00:23:45,657 --> 00:23:47,658
(Next course up: steps by the waterfall)

623
00:23:47,659 --> 00:23:50,628
On the way back up,
we can hold onto this rope.

624
00:23:50,830 --> 00:23:52,364
You've got to be kidding me!

625
00:23:52,365 --> 00:23:53,231
Nope, totally serious!

626
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:55,967
There is no way to avoid
getting soaked here.

627
00:23:55,968 --> 00:23:57,135
(Passing through the refreshing path)

628
00:23:57,803 --> 00:23:58,736
I think we're almost at the bottom.

629
00:23:58,737 --> 00:24:00,271
We're practically there!

630
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,539
Yes, we're really close!

631
00:24:01,841 --> 00:24:02,875
Only about 5 minutes away.

632
00:24:02,876 --> 00:24:04,042
Sounds great!

633
00:24:04,043 --> 00:24:05,443
(Only a few minutes
until finally seeing the waterfall)

634
00:24:06,312 --> 00:24:08,346
This is the rest stop.

635
00:24:08,347 --> 00:24:09,314
Got it.

636
00:24:09,548 --> 00:24:12,550
If you need to catch your breath,
you can take a breather here.

637
00:24:12,551 --> 00:24:14,819
- Okay!
- No problem.

638
00:24:15,588 --> 00:24:17,389
I feel like...

639
00:24:17,823 --> 00:24:19,390
we're completely boxed in.

640
00:24:20,025 --> 00:24:20,791
Right?

641
00:24:20,792 --> 00:24:22,493
(Cliffs surround the rest area.)

642
00:24:22,661 --> 00:24:25,263
- We literally just climbed down that way.
- That way?

643
00:24:25,497 --> 00:24:27,798
Looking at it from here,
it looks terrifying!

644
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:30,501
- It looks spectacular, though!
- Totally!

645
00:24:30,502 --> 00:24:32,203
(Steps by the cliff look menacing
from this distance.)

646
00:24:32,538 --> 00:24:33,738
Shall we keep moving?

647
00:24:33,739 --> 00:24:34,939
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

648
00:24:35,441 --> 00:24:36,607
Let's do it!

649
00:24:39,945 --> 00:24:41,346
Look, there's a little rainbow over there!

650
00:24:41,347 --> 00:24:42,346
It's a rainbow!

651
00:24:42,347 --> 00:24:43,247
You're so right!

652
00:24:43,883 --> 00:24:45,883
There's a rainbow right over there!

653
00:24:46,252 --> 00:24:49,621
(Rainbow created by the waterfall)

654
00:24:49,955 --> 00:24:51,088
I definitely want a picture of that!

655
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:56,494
(Walking for another five minutes)

656
00:24:57,162 --> 00:24:58,863
Welcome to the jungle!

657
00:24:58,864 --> 00:24:59,864
(Finally seeing some flat ground)

658
00:24:59,865 --> 00:25:00,831
Another one?

659
00:25:00,832 --> 00:25:03,101
Another bridge!

660
00:25:03,102 --> 00:25:05,936
It feels like someone is misting my face.

661
00:25:06,739 --> 00:25:08,673
Yeah, I totally feel it!

662
00:25:09,742 --> 00:25:15,513
(Water droplets fall like rain)

663
00:25:15,915 --> 00:25:17,415
Look, they're completely soaked!

664
00:25:18,017 --> 00:25:20,118
Drenched from head to toe!

665
00:25:20,119 --> 00:25:22,520
(People walking back completely soaked)

666
00:25:22,521 --> 00:25:24,456
Literally everyone walking back
is soaking wet.

667
00:25:24,457 --> 00:25:26,558
I guess you can't dodge it
once you head in.

668
00:25:29,328 --> 00:25:30,595
It's stunning!

669
00:25:30,931 --> 00:25:31,729
So gorgeous!

670
00:25:31,730 --> 00:25:33,931
(Sun shining through the cliffs)

671
00:25:35,968 --> 00:25:37,302
It's a full canyon.

672
00:25:37,503 --> 00:25:39,804
The waterfall is tucked
behind these cliffs.

673
00:25:39,805 --> 00:25:42,340
- So it's just around the bend?
- Yep!

674
00:25:42,341 --> 00:25:43,875
(Waterfall waits beyond the canyon.)

675
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:46,510
The falls are right around the corner!

676
00:25:47,714 --> 00:25:49,647
Another bridge to cross!

677
00:26:02,861 --> 00:26:03,894
Wait, how are we supposed to cross that?

678
00:26:04,129 --> 00:26:06,397
As the saying goes,
enemies always meet on a narrow bridge.

679
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:08,232
It's ridiculously narrow!

680
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,867
Yeah, it's basically a strip of wood!

681
00:26:10,469 --> 00:26:11,369
(The ultimate bottleneck)

682
00:26:12,137 --> 00:26:13,404
- Let's go for it!
- Coming.

683
00:26:13,539 --> 00:26:15,606
Take it slow and be careful!

684
00:26:16,075 --> 00:26:18,410
All right, let's roll!

685
00:26:20,479 --> 00:26:22,647
This is way scarier than I expected.

686
00:26:22,915 --> 00:26:25,283
Does it sway?

687
00:26:26,251 --> 00:26:28,219
It's way freakier than it looks!

688
00:26:28,220 --> 00:26:29,620
All right, here we go!

689
00:26:29,621 --> 00:26:31,689
(Younger members stride across
without any problem.)

690
00:26:31,957 --> 00:26:32,857
Wait, was I the only one terrified?

691
00:26:33,260 --> 00:26:34,693
- No way!
- I wasn't scared at all!

692
00:26:34,694 --> 00:26:37,062
- Wait, I mean, I was terrified!
- Right?

693
00:26:37,063 --> 00:26:37,896
That was a breeze!

694
00:26:38,130 --> 00:26:38,963
Piece of cake!

695
00:26:39,899 --> 00:26:40,965
How is he just walking like that?

696
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:43,768
(Fin runs across the bridge.)

697
00:26:43,769 --> 00:26:44,635
He literally sprinted across!

698
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:47,171
- Easy peasy!
- Easy peasy squeezy.

699
00:26:47,172 --> 00:26:48,339
Yep, easy peasy for me!

700
00:26:48,340 --> 00:26:50,974
(Walking across the canyon)

701
00:26:50,975 --> 00:26:52,676
I'm pretty sure we're about to get soaked.

702
00:26:55,647 --> 00:26:57,448
I hear the water!

703
00:26:58,817 --> 00:27:00,484
(In awe)

704
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:03,888
Be ready.

705
00:27:04,723 --> 00:27:06,157
This is unbelievable.

706
00:27:06,325 --> 00:27:07,892
It's incredible!

707
00:27:11,997 --> 00:27:15,399
- Look!
- It's so breathtaking up close!

708
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:17,134
It's purely magical.

709
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:18,135
(Finally seeing the Thousand Waterfalls)

710
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:19,036
Unreal.

711
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:27,445
(Rendered speechless by the sight)

712
00:27:28,647 --> 00:27:32,183
(Younger members acting out again)

713
00:27:32,418 --> 00:27:34,285
Welcome to Tumpak Sewu Waterfall!

714
00:27:34,286 --> 00:27:36,420
Thank you!

715
00:27:36,421 --> 00:27:37,855
This is out of this world!

716
00:27:39,391 --> 00:27:40,224
What do you think?

717
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:42,460
- Wonderful, right?
- It's crazy.

718
00:27:43,729 --> 00:27:45,396
It's like a tropical Niagara Falls!

719
00:27:46,198 --> 00:27:48,933
Do you get to see this view every day?

720
00:27:48,934 --> 00:27:50,101
Yeah, every single day!

721
00:27:50,936 --> 00:27:52,469
You are so lucky!

722
00:27:53,872 --> 00:27:58,776
(Precarious footings)

723
00:28:00,012 --> 00:28:00,979
This is insane!

724
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:04,482
(Crossing the last bridge with a racket)

725
00:28:04,917 --> 00:28:06,651
(More water droplets as they cross)

726
00:28:06,652 --> 00:28:08,620
- We got this!
- Whoa, look at the water here...

727
00:28:08,621 --> 00:28:10,521
The water spray here is insane!

728
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:13,524
So this is why everyone was soaked!

729
00:28:16,095 --> 00:28:17,220
It feels so refreshing, though!

730
00:28:19,098 --> 00:28:20,098
This is spectacular!

731
00:28:20,099 --> 00:28:24,836
(Mist created by the waterfall)

732
00:28:24,837 --> 00:28:26,871
There's actually a hidden gem right here.

733
00:28:26,872 --> 00:28:29,541
If you look straight up at the sky,
the cliffs form a heart.

734
00:28:30,742 --> 00:28:32,810
He's totally right!
You can actually see a heart!

735
00:28:33,679 --> 00:28:34,746
That is so cool!

736
00:28:36,594 --> 00:28:37,794
Wow.

737
00:28:37,955 --> 00:28:39,007
Be careful, right?

738
00:28:39,008 --> 00:28:40,296
(Walking up closer)

739
00:28:40,753 --> 00:28:43,187
We're the salmon squad!

740
00:28:44,022 --> 00:28:47,458
The whole theme of our journey is salmon!

741
00:28:47,459 --> 00:28:48,926
Theme of salmon!

742
00:28:49,928 --> 00:28:51,962
Let's swim upstream!

743
00:28:51,963 --> 00:28:53,864
(Salmon girls climbing)

744
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:56,067
I'm taking you to a gorgeous spot!

745
00:28:56,068 --> 00:28:57,168
Awesome!

746
00:28:57,936 --> 00:28:58,769
Almost there!

747
00:28:58,770 --> 00:29:01,071
We're almost there!

748
00:29:04,576 --> 00:29:06,143
Just look at the falls from right here!

749
00:29:07,846 --> 00:29:09,513
We're so close!

750
00:29:12,317 --> 00:29:14,485
I legitimately feel like
I'm in Jurassic Park.

751
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:20,691
They could film Jurassic Park right here!

752
00:29:20,692 --> 00:29:22,592
They just need to put dinosaurs here.

753
00:29:22,593 --> 00:29:23,828
(Like a scene in a movie)

754
00:29:23,829 --> 00:29:24,730
(Moved)

755
00:29:24,731 --> 00:29:25,696
It's so breathtaking.

756
00:29:27,533 --> 00:29:29,500
- Truly magnificent!
- Indeed.

757
00:29:30,335 --> 00:29:31,468
Did we really climb down
from way up there?

758
00:29:31,469 --> 00:29:34,772
Yeah, all the way from the very top!
Right, somewhere up there.

759
00:29:37,543 --> 00:29:38,977
This is mind-blowing.

760
00:29:39,378 --> 00:29:40,779
A photo could never do this justice.

761
00:29:40,780 --> 00:29:42,317
- Not even close.
- Way more magnificent.

762
00:29:42,614 --> 00:29:44,582
This is pure majesty.

763
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:45,916
(The great nature manifests
in the huge waterfall.)

764
00:29:46,451 --> 00:29:49,587
I feel like the rushing water is...

765
00:29:49,588 --> 00:29:51,021
washing all my stress away.

766
00:29:52,124 --> 00:29:55,259
Fun fact! This place only opened
to the public...

767
00:29:55,561 --> 00:29:57,661
fairly recently.

768
00:29:57,662 --> 00:30:00,964
It officially opened in 2015.
That was 11 years ago.

769
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:11,176
- Really?
- Yeah.

770
00:30:11,203 --> 00:30:15,480
But it was a hit
from the moment it opened.

771
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:17,481
- A lot of people came.
- Yeah, many people.

772
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:19,051
Many people came here.

773
00:30:19,409 --> 00:30:22,087
How did they not see this place
becoming a tourist attraction?

774
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:25,590
- Wow, interesting.
- Interesting, right?

775
00:30:26,291 --> 00:30:27,559
A rainbow.

776
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:29,106
- A rainbow?
- Where?

777
00:30:29,107 --> 00:30:30,762
- There's a rainbow over there.
- I found it.

778
00:30:30,827 --> 00:30:32,360
Rainbow!

779
00:30:33,533 --> 00:30:35,033
Wow, a rainbow.

780
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:39,642
Okay, let's go down there
to take a picture.

781
00:30:39,643 --> 00:30:41,106
Okay!

782
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:46,167
(Careful)

783
00:30:47,045 --> 00:30:49,247
It's harder when you go down.

784
00:30:50,287 --> 00:30:52,617
I really feel like...

785
00:30:52,951 --> 00:30:55,354
I'm growing through this trip.

786
00:30:55,787 --> 00:30:58,890
- What did you grow into?
- A strong woman.

787
00:30:58,891 --> 00:31:00,492
Oh, a strong woman.

788
00:31:00,747 --> 00:31:02,928
Into a woman who is capable
of doing things on her own.

789
00:31:03,381 --> 00:31:06,631
I think you already were.

790
00:31:07,634 --> 00:31:11,681
(The lower they go,
the wilder the spray gets.)

791
00:31:11,988 --> 00:31:13,438
Wow, it's right there.

792
00:31:13,972 --> 00:31:16,565
- How about we take a picture here?
- Yeah.

793
00:31:16,659 --> 00:31:18,377
Let's take a group picture.

794
00:31:19,044 --> 00:31:21,346
You can really feel it up close.

795
00:31:21,646 --> 00:31:23,515
You can feel the mist!

796
00:31:23,566 --> 00:31:25,566
Natural mist.

797
00:31:26,533 --> 00:31:27,819
It's so...

798
00:31:28,220 --> 00:31:29,646
hard to keep your eyes open!

799
00:31:30,922 --> 00:31:33,625
We're basically in a pool.

800
00:31:33,900 --> 00:31:35,193
Underwater.

801
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:38,263
- Wow.
- Wow!

802
00:31:38,873 --> 00:31:42,900
(Mist spraying everywhere)

803
00:31:43,335 --> 00:31:45,070
It's so windy.

804
00:31:46,772 --> 00:31:48,707
Oh, come on!

805
00:31:49,411 --> 00:31:50,842
Seriously!

806
00:31:51,751 --> 00:31:53,245
This is why people get wet.

807
00:31:53,246 --> 00:31:55,447
I thought people went into the waterfall.

808
00:31:56,077 --> 00:31:57,883
He's really good at taking pictures.

809
00:31:57,884 --> 00:32:01,677
(The camera gets soaked,
and so does the shot.)

810
00:32:02,077 --> 00:32:05,764
I've never been to a photo spot
that blasts you with this much water.

811
00:32:05,765 --> 00:32:08,460
- I know, right?
- Yes.

812
00:32:08,537 --> 00:32:11,430
But it's so majestic,
you can't really complain.

813
00:32:12,614 --> 00:32:14,800
The price you pay
to see a waterfall this big!

814
00:32:14,820 --> 00:32:16,001
You're right.

815
00:32:16,147 --> 00:32:18,537
- Even if you can't keep your eyes open!
- You're right.

816
00:32:18,538 --> 00:32:20,574
(To behold the waterfall,
one must endure the spray.)

817
00:32:21,006 --> 00:32:23,942
So this is what they mean
by "little drops add up."

818
00:32:24,209 --> 00:32:27,078
- These are little drops, right?
- Are you sure they're little?

819
00:32:29,381 --> 00:32:30,682
Maybe it's not so little.

820
00:32:33,018 --> 00:32:35,469
I mean, it does feel like heavy rain.

821
00:32:35,470 --> 00:32:37,589
We're soaked.

822
00:32:37,749 --> 00:32:40,125
We need to take a picture.

823
00:32:40,126 --> 00:32:41,526
Let's just take one like this.

824
00:32:42,036 --> 00:32:43,728
- Right now?
- We look fine, though!

825
00:32:43,783 --> 00:32:45,530
- Yeah?
- Oh, we're fine.

826
00:32:47,254 --> 00:32:49,934
(Moist)

827
00:32:50,334 --> 00:32:52,334
I actually like how natural we look.

828
00:32:52,335 --> 00:32:53,438
Yeah.

829
00:32:54,021 --> 00:32:56,021
Feels very natural, right?

830
00:32:56,022 --> 00:32:58,288
(You do look like you belong in the wild.)

831
00:32:59,044 --> 00:33:03,615
You know what's so funny?
Everyone here is like...

832
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:05,048
(Rub)

833
00:33:05,155 --> 00:33:07,155
(Sparkle)

834
00:33:07,262 --> 00:33:08,920
- Yeah.
- You're right.

835
00:33:08,921 --> 00:33:12,235
(People really come alive for photos.)

836
00:33:12,435 --> 00:33:13,074
Yes!

837
00:33:13,075 --> 00:33:14,482
(Rub)

838
00:33:14,995 --> 00:33:16,302
(Sparkle)

839
00:33:16,602 --> 00:33:18,063
They're all wiping their cameras too.

840
00:33:18,195 --> 00:33:19,698
(Travel is the click
between a splash and a sparkle.)

841
00:33:19,762 --> 00:33:21,099
It's reality.

842
00:33:22,534 --> 00:33:24,669
- Our turn.
- Yes, okay.

843
00:33:24,745 --> 00:33:25,704
Let's go.

844
00:33:26,638 --> 00:33:29,541
It's okay for you four to stand
together here.

845
00:33:29,542 --> 00:33:31,258
Okay.

846
00:33:31,625 --> 00:33:34,012
In 3, 2, 1.

847
00:33:34,691 --> 00:33:37,618
(Looking somewhat helpless)

848
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:40,018
Okay, I'll take a video too.

849
00:33:40,078 --> 00:33:42,387
Put your hands together like this.

850
00:33:42,388 --> 00:33:44,890
Cover the camera, then raise your hands
when I give you the signal.

851
00:33:44,891 --> 00:33:46,491
Okay, perfect!

852
00:33:46,851 --> 00:33:49,094
One, two, three.

853
00:33:49,483 --> 00:33:52,655
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

854
00:33:52,888 --> 00:33:53,631
My bad.

855
00:33:53,632 --> 00:33:55,567
I'm so sorry!

856
00:33:55,665 --> 00:33:57,135
- I didn't mean to grab you.
- No, it's fine.

857
00:33:57,736 --> 00:33:59,371
(Too close for comfort)

858
00:33:59,525 --> 00:34:01,006
I'm sorry I grabbed you.

859
00:34:01,306 --> 00:34:03,153
We'll take one more.

860
00:34:03,154 --> 00:34:05,377
- One more.
- Much closer.

861
00:34:06,033 --> 00:34:07,579
One, two, three.

862
00:34:07,606 --> 00:34:08,747
(Roar)

863
00:34:08,766 --> 00:34:09,781
(Screech)

864
00:34:10,826 --> 00:34:12,973
(What are they doing?)

865
00:34:13,619 --> 00:34:15,053
(Roar)

866
00:34:17,873 --> 00:34:19,824
- You're so funny.
- She's finally gone mad.

867
00:34:19,825 --> 00:34:21,259
So funny.

868
00:34:21,693 --> 00:34:24,051
I want to take a photo in there.

869
00:34:24,052 --> 00:34:25,430
Sure. Let's go.

870
00:34:26,057 --> 00:34:28,611
One, two, three.

871
00:34:30,804 --> 00:34:33,071
She seems to be feeling better.
Thank goodness.

872
00:34:33,244 --> 00:34:35,073
She's got enough energy for photos now.

873
00:34:37,015 --> 00:34:39,009
(Scorpion)

874
00:34:58,369 --> 00:34:59,698
- Really?
- Yeah.

875
00:34:59,729 --> 00:35:02,133
- I've never taken one here.
- Really?

876
00:35:02,209 --> 00:35:03,015
Really?

877
00:35:03,016 --> 00:35:04,402
- We can take one for you!
- Come on!

878
00:35:04,403 --> 00:35:06,805
Give me your phone. Okay, let's go!

879
00:35:06,901 --> 00:35:09,074
- Strike a pose!
- Okay.

880
00:35:09,674 --> 00:35:10,508
Let's go!

881
00:35:10,509 --> 00:35:12,310
You're going to take a picture of me?

882
00:35:12,328 --> 00:35:13,211
Only you!

883
00:35:13,212 --> 00:35:14,546
- Only me?
- Yeah!

884
00:35:15,614 --> 00:35:16,514
Over here?

885
00:35:17,162 --> 00:35:18,282
Yeah, perfect!

886
00:35:20,774 --> 00:35:25,574
- Yes!
- Oh, my goodness!

887
00:35:25,714 --> 00:35:27,559
- Let's take a video.
- Video.

888
00:35:27,560 --> 00:35:28,760
- Video?
- Video!

889
00:35:28,761 --> 00:35:29,894
Video.

890
00:35:29,895 --> 00:35:33,214
(His first proper pose here)

891
00:35:33,574 --> 00:35:35,260
(Focused)

892
00:35:35,261 --> 00:35:36,434
Okay!

893
00:35:36,501 --> 00:35:38,737
Okay. Thank you, guys!

894
00:35:38,934 --> 00:35:39,877
Perfect!

895
00:35:39,878 --> 00:35:40,745
Be careful.

896
00:35:40,746 --> 00:35:42,340
Thank you for taking a picture for me.

897
00:35:42,341 --> 00:35:44,441
- Is this your first time?
- Yes.

898
00:35:44,442 --> 00:35:45,877
- Really?
- Really.

899
00:35:46,378 --> 00:35:48,780
I just take pictures for people.

900
00:35:48,958 --> 00:35:50,498
- Every day.
- Every day.

901
00:35:50,551 --> 00:35:54,144
- You only take pictures for others.
- Yes.

902
00:35:54,631 --> 00:35:57,971
(Excitedly checking the photos)

903
00:35:58,038 --> 00:35:59,758
The picture is good.

904
00:36:01,564 --> 00:36:03,128
(Instantly gets the perfect shot!)

905
00:36:03,129 --> 00:36:05,463
The pictures look great.

906
00:36:05,562 --> 00:36:07,232
Wow, thank you.

907
00:36:08,433 --> 00:36:10,433
- Do you like it?
- Yeah, I like it.

908
00:36:10,434 --> 00:36:12,270
- Thank you.
- Good for you.

909
00:36:13,381 --> 00:36:15,381
Goodbye, waterfall!

910
00:36:15,382 --> 00:36:17,042
Goodbye!

911
00:36:17,361 --> 00:36:19,044
- See you again.
- See you.

912
00:36:19,045 --> 00:36:20,181
See you again!

913
00:36:22,342 --> 00:36:23,581
That was fun.

914
00:36:23,701 --> 00:36:25,617
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

915
00:36:28,299 --> 00:36:30,225
Okay, 500 steps again.

916
00:36:30,279 --> 00:36:31,489
Five hundred again.

917
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:33,491
That's 1,000 total.

918
00:36:33,492 --> 00:36:36,661
- We can do it.
- Yes, we can!

919
00:36:37,066 --> 00:36:38,897
Power through!

920
00:36:39,646 --> 00:36:41,566
- Power through!
- Power through!

921
00:36:41,992 --> 00:36:44,469
- Power through!
- Power through!

922
00:36:44,872 --> 00:36:47,072
Why are we suddenly doing squats?

923
00:36:47,719 --> 00:36:49,741
Stairway to heaven, real-life edition!

924
00:36:55,913 --> 00:36:59,587
(Climbing their way up the falls)

925
00:37:00,852 --> 00:37:03,054
Here comes the steep part.

926
00:37:04,838 --> 00:37:07,759
Never thought I'd be
rock climbing in my life.

927
00:37:08,871 --> 00:37:11,045
(Inching)

928
00:37:13,378 --> 00:37:14,299
(Sighing)

929
00:37:14,836 --> 00:37:15,667
(Panting)

930
00:37:16,262 --> 00:37:17,135
(Sighing)

931
00:37:17,362 --> 00:37:19,871
Seriously, this is harder
than the Himalayas!

932
00:37:23,876 --> 00:37:27,567
(A lot to process)

933
00:37:27,734 --> 00:37:29,948
Let's go.

934
00:37:30,487 --> 00:37:31,950
Hurry up.

935
00:37:32,907 --> 00:37:34,352
I'm sorry, Mom.

936
00:37:35,220 --> 00:37:36,554
I'll be a good girl.

937
00:37:37,205 --> 00:37:38,690
I think we're almost there.

938
00:37:38,691 --> 00:37:40,492
Was that the end of the steps?

939
00:37:41,052 --> 00:37:42,293
We've come a long way.

940
00:37:42,412 --> 00:37:43,728
We really have.

941
00:37:45,725 --> 00:37:47,665
- How much longer?
- A little bit more.

942
00:37:47,666 --> 00:37:48,700
A little bit more!

943
00:37:48,701 --> 00:37:50,068
- Wow!
- A little bit more, okay!

944
00:37:50,368 --> 00:37:51,603
Thank you so much.

945
00:37:51,604 --> 00:37:53,275
(We're almost there!)

946
00:37:53,276 --> 00:37:54,639
Just a little bit more.

947
00:37:54,990 --> 00:37:57,256
We can do it.

948
00:37:57,257 --> 00:37:58,610
We really are almost there.

949
00:37:58,630 --> 00:38:00,945
Okay! At last!

950
00:38:01,770 --> 00:38:04,382
Okay.

951
00:38:04,783 --> 00:38:06,217
I can smell durian.

952
00:38:07,110 --> 00:38:09,569
(We did it!)

953
00:38:09,603 --> 00:38:11,456
Thank you.

954
00:38:11,457 --> 00:38:14,842
(As if they just finished a marathon)

955
00:38:15,794 --> 00:38:17,794
She's opening it for us.

956
00:38:18,456 --> 00:38:19,664
Temptation!

957
00:38:19,863 --> 00:38:21,299
How about some orange juice?

958
00:38:21,679 --> 00:38:22,767
I want this.

959
00:38:22,835 --> 00:38:23,796
Mangosteen?

960
00:38:23,797 --> 00:38:25,370
- Go ahead.
- Is that mangosteen?

961
00:38:25,963 --> 00:38:27,105
- They're really good.
- Do you want some?

962
00:38:27,705 --> 00:38:30,275
- Let's get something to drink.
- Yeah, let's do that.

963
00:38:30,387 --> 00:38:31,476
Let's sit here.

964
00:38:31,477 --> 00:38:33,947
(A well-earned break after the climb)

965
00:38:34,447 --> 00:38:37,307
(Taking a seat at the rest stop)

966
00:38:37,685 --> 00:38:40,051
I'm going to ask if they have iced coffee.

967
00:38:40,919 --> 00:38:43,054
- Do they have iced coffee?
- Yes.

968
00:38:43,979 --> 00:38:45,089
I'll pay!

969
00:38:45,090 --> 00:38:46,423
(Opening the wallet over iced coffee)

970
00:38:46,437 --> 00:38:48,339
- One iced coffee?
- Yes.

971
00:38:48,371 --> 00:38:49,330
Choose from there.

972
00:38:49,337 --> 00:38:51,396
Oh, you can choose from there.

973
00:38:51,953 --> 00:38:52,819
(Once you choose what you want,)

974
00:38:52,820 --> 00:38:53,871
Wow, that's so cool.

975
00:38:54,777 --> 00:38:56,324
(Shaking)

976
00:38:56,784 --> 00:38:59,584
(they make it on the spot.)

977
00:38:59,884 --> 00:39:01,539
Oh, and...

978
00:39:01,571 --> 00:39:02,941
I learned the importance of exercise.

979
00:39:02,942 --> 00:39:04,075
Do they have chocolate?

980
00:39:04,424 --> 00:39:05,476
- Chocolate?
- Yeah.

981
00:39:05,477 --> 00:39:06,845
I think they have chocolate milk.

982
00:39:06,913 --> 00:39:08,513
- Chocolate.
- But I have some.

983
00:39:08,847 --> 00:39:11,939
- I always pack some for my guests.
- Oh!

984
00:39:12,386 --> 00:39:13,418
Really?

985
00:39:13,526 --> 00:39:15,066
But it's not a big one.

986
00:39:15,393 --> 00:39:16,421
No problem.

987
00:39:16,551 --> 00:39:19,357
- I need something sweet.
- Something sweet.

988
00:39:19,491 --> 00:39:20,724
Wow, what's that?

989
00:39:21,524 --> 00:39:24,329
These are just like the ones I had
when I was little.

990
00:39:24,330 --> 00:39:25,471
What is this?

991
00:39:25,472 --> 00:39:26,945
Do you know what these are?

992
00:39:26,946 --> 00:39:28,700
I think I know.

993
00:39:28,792 --> 00:39:31,736
You just suck it like this.
I had these when I was a kid.

994
00:39:31,737 --> 00:39:32,737
Really?

995
00:39:32,778 --> 00:39:33,872
This stuff's really good.

996
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:35,607
It's addictive.

997
00:39:37,637 --> 00:39:40,003
(Sucking)

998
00:39:40,417 --> 00:39:41,403
(Nom)

999
00:39:41,503 --> 00:39:42,914
It's exactly how I remember it.

1000
00:39:43,214 --> 00:39:45,383
Just like you remember.

1001
00:39:46,017 --> 00:39:47,652
- I like it.
- You like it?

1002
00:39:47,653 --> 00:39:48,653
I have more.

1003
00:39:49,593 --> 00:39:50,855
Mmm!

1004
00:39:50,966 --> 00:39:52,056
- It's good.
- Right?

1005
00:39:52,057 --> 00:39:53,266
(Sweet)

1006
00:39:53,440 --> 00:39:56,261
It tastes just like the chocolate
we used to buy as kids.

1007
00:39:56,794 --> 00:39:58,363
I want to buy a whole tub of this.

1008
00:39:59,286 --> 00:40:00,528
- You like it that much?
- Me too.

1009
00:40:00,532 --> 00:40:03,267
I'm not saying it's gourmet.

1010
00:40:03,268 --> 00:40:04,702
- But nostalgic.
- It just tastes like pure nostalgia.

1011
00:40:04,703 --> 00:40:06,504
It's my favorite childhood chocolate.

1012
00:40:06,674 --> 00:40:09,173
(Thanks to Fin,
she's fully recharged with happiness.)

1013
00:40:09,641 --> 00:40:10,674
Coffee's here!

1014
00:40:11,476 --> 00:40:12,743
The coffee is here!

1015
00:40:12,768 --> 00:40:14,344
(The iced coffee arrived right on cue.)

1016
00:40:14,479 --> 00:40:16,080
How do you say "cheers" in Indonesian?

1017
00:40:16,581 --> 00:40:18,649
- Cheers.
- Just "cheers"?

1018
00:40:18,650 --> 00:40:19,550
Yes!

1019
00:40:19,551 --> 00:40:20,775
We say, "Geonbae" in Korea.

1020
00:40:20,776 --> 00:40:22,520
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

1021
00:40:22,521 --> 00:40:25,022
(A sip after the toast)

1022
00:40:25,356 --> 00:40:26,222
It's so good.

1023
00:40:29,961 --> 00:40:30,761
So refreshing.

1024
00:40:30,762 --> 00:40:32,896
(A sweet little breather)

1025
00:40:34,299 --> 00:40:35,116
Guys.

1026
00:40:35,533 --> 00:40:37,334
I'm going to edit the video for you,

1027
00:40:37,945 --> 00:40:40,304
starting with footage
from when we set off.

1028
00:40:40,305 --> 00:40:43,173
I'll put together a Reel
and send it over later.

1029
00:40:43,174 --> 00:40:45,542
Thank you so much!

1030
00:40:45,810 --> 00:40:46,710
That is so sweet of you!

1031
00:40:46,711 --> 00:40:48,812
Where are you guys headed next?

1032
00:40:49,514 --> 00:40:51,048
- Volcano.
- Cemoro Lawang.

1033
00:40:51,382 --> 00:40:52,382
Cemoro Lawang!

1034
00:40:52,383 --> 00:40:54,751
You're going to Mount Bromo!

1035
00:40:54,752 --> 00:40:56,319
- That's the absolute best spot.
- Is it really that great?

1036
00:40:56,554 --> 00:40:59,055
It's the true icon of Java.

1037
00:40:59,492 --> 00:41:02,759
(Mount Bromo is one
of Java's famous landmarks.)

1038
00:41:02,760 --> 00:41:04,828
Is there anywhere else you recommend?

1039
00:41:05,063 --> 00:41:06,497
Anywhere else?

1040
00:41:06,631 --> 00:41:09,433
I know an amazing sunrise viewpoint.

1041
00:41:09,434 --> 00:41:11,468
It's called King Kong Hill.

1042
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:12,803
King Kong?

1043
00:41:13,238 --> 00:41:14,104
King Kong Hill?

1044
00:41:14,873 --> 00:41:17,375
It's hands down the best spot for sunrise.

1045
00:41:17,412 --> 00:41:20,601
You should head up there
tomorrow to catch it.

1046
00:41:20,626 --> 00:41:23,179
It's an incredible view.

1047
00:41:23,180 --> 00:41:24,180
- Is it really pretty?
- Absolutely.

1048
00:41:24,181 --> 00:41:25,973
All right, I trust your taste.

1049
00:41:26,095 --> 00:41:28,989
- Definitely check it out tomorrow.
- Will do!

1050
00:41:29,014 --> 00:41:29,953
(Going with Fin's top pick)

1051
00:41:30,856 --> 00:41:33,824
Guys, I actually have
a little souvenir for you.

1052
00:41:34,092 --> 00:41:35,626
So you can remember this place!

1053
00:41:35,627 --> 00:41:36,693
(Fin prepared a surprise gift.)

1054
00:41:36,828 --> 00:41:38,129
Is this a magnet?

1055
00:41:38,130 --> 00:41:40,230
- I made it myself!
- Oh, wow!

1056
00:41:40,231 --> 00:41:41,231
It's a handmade magnet!

1057
00:41:41,532 --> 00:41:42,832
Look, a magnet!

1058
00:41:42,833 --> 00:41:43,700
(Then...)

1059
00:41:47,472 --> 00:41:48,338
(In a daze)

1060
00:41:49,204 --> 00:41:50,457
<i>Super attraction</i>

1061
00:41:50,875 --> 00:41:52,375
His battery is completely drained.

1062
00:41:53,328 --> 00:41:54,879
Here, the... Yes.

1063
00:41:54,880 --> 00:41:55,779
(Total social burnout)

1064
00:41:56,581 --> 00:41:58,144
- Are you okay?
- Yes, I'm okay.

1065
00:41:58,145 --> 00:42:00,584
Fin is so sweet.
He just goes along with everything.

1066
00:42:01,152 --> 00:42:03,153
(The determined introvert)

1067
00:42:03,888 --> 00:42:05,121
This represents Tumpak Sewu.

1068
00:42:10,161 --> 00:42:11,895
(Gift showcase time)

1069
00:42:11,896 --> 00:42:12,829
It's gorgeous!

1070
00:42:14,098 --> 00:42:18,101
(A heartfelt souvenir handmade by Fin)

1071
00:42:18,836 --> 00:42:19,936
Don't forget me!

1072
00:42:21,406 --> 00:42:23,040
Don't you forget about us, either!

1073
00:42:23,041 --> 00:42:24,441
Of course not!

1074
00:42:25,410 --> 00:42:27,878
Thank you for traveling with me today.

1075
00:42:28,446 --> 00:42:31,515
(Fin and the girls
say their goodbyes here.)

1076
00:42:31,516 --> 00:42:32,827
Thank you!

1077
00:42:34,285 --> 00:42:36,753
Come with us to Mount Bromo!

1078
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:39,622
- Come along!
- Let's go together!

1079
00:42:40,025 --> 00:42:41,992
I wish I could, but I have to work!

1080
00:42:41,993 --> 00:42:42,959
Thank you, though!

1081
00:42:43,127 --> 00:42:45,862
Thank you for making this
such an unforgettable experience!

1082
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:47,664
- Bye!
- Goodbye!

1083
00:42:47,665 --> 00:42:49,499
- See you next time!
- See you again!

1084
00:42:49,500 --> 00:42:51,077
(Parting on such a happy note)

1085
00:42:51,102 --> 00:42:52,235
That was seriously so much fun.

1086
00:42:53,137 --> 00:42:55,872
I think I'm just perpetually damp now.

1087
00:42:55,873 --> 00:42:56,773
Seriously.

1088
00:42:57,075 --> 00:42:58,909
I haven't been completely dry all day.

1089
00:42:59,777 --> 00:43:00,741
(Changing out of their drenched clothes)

1090
00:43:00,742 --> 00:43:03,384
- Can I borrow one of your T-shirts?
- My pleasure.

1091
00:43:04,082 --> 00:43:05,349
I'm so excited!

1092
00:43:05,618 --> 00:43:08,242
Smells amazing in here! Hello!

1093
00:43:08,486 --> 00:43:10,497
(Grabbing a quick bite at a nearby spot)

1094
00:43:10,579 --> 00:43:11,756
Hello!

1095
00:43:12,356 --> 00:43:13,423
Wait, hold on!

1096
00:43:14,726 --> 00:43:18,028
Fin already finished editing our Reel
and sent it over!

1097
00:43:18,029 --> 00:43:19,262
How did he do that so fast?

1098
00:43:20,398 --> 00:43:21,665
Let's open it!

1099
00:43:21,666 --> 00:43:23,700
(Unveiling the Reel Fin put together)

1100
00:43:23,701 --> 00:43:25,569
(File name: To My Lovely Friends)

1101
00:43:25,570 --> 00:43:27,404
(Directed by Fin)

1102
00:43:27,939 --> 00:43:32,477
(It opens with a cinematic slow-mo shot.)

1103
00:43:32,478 --> 00:43:34,411
I love that he put it in slow motion!

1104
00:43:35,947 --> 00:43:37,047
This turned out so cool!

1105
00:43:37,048 --> 00:43:38,649
(Tumpak Sewu appears right on cue.)

1106
00:43:39,083 --> 00:43:41,718
(Followed by their epic descent)

1107
00:43:41,719 --> 00:43:43,586
Look, we're still hiking down!

1108
00:43:43,855 --> 00:43:45,189
You're dancing in this part, too!

1109
00:43:46,090 --> 00:43:47,557
He framed this so well.

1110
00:43:50,928 --> 00:43:52,528
The music drops right on beat!

1111
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:57,100
- It's already such a great memory.
- Totally!

1112
00:44:06,277 --> 00:44:07,110
This is seriously...

1113
00:44:07,912 --> 00:44:11,382
(A flashy, dynamic finale)

1114
00:44:11,383 --> 00:44:12,249
Won Ji!

1115
00:44:13,384 --> 00:44:15,385
(Peak satisfaction)

1116
00:44:15,553 --> 00:44:17,020
He even kept that part in?

1117
00:44:17,622 --> 00:44:19,523
Because we had such a blast with it!

1118
00:44:20,226 --> 00:44:21,592
He did an amazing job with this.

1119
00:44:21,593 --> 00:44:22,893
I'm obsessed with the ending!

1120
00:44:22,894 --> 00:44:25,495
It's so fun. Every cut is gold!

1121
00:44:25,496 --> 00:44:26,496
I know, right?

1122
00:44:35,173 --> 00:44:38,175
You've got a real eye for this.
Keep it up!

1123
00:44:38,676 --> 00:44:40,443
I genuinely love it.
He did such a fantastic job.

1124
00:44:44,412 --> 00:44:45,482
(Love it)

1125
00:44:45,483 --> 00:44:46,316
This food hits the spot!

1126
00:44:46,317 --> 00:44:48,819
(Happily diving back into their meal)

1127
00:44:49,253 --> 00:44:50,053
Wait, oh no.

1128
00:44:50,690 --> 00:44:51,922
I completely forgot to book
our place for tonight!

1129
00:44:53,391 --> 00:44:57,462
(Having so much fun
they forgot the most crucial detail.)

1130
00:44:57,962 --> 00:45:02,432
Won Ji usually locks down our lodging,

1131
00:45:03,034 --> 00:45:04,601
so let me handle it this time!

1132
00:45:04,602 --> 00:45:05,702
Really?

1133
00:45:05,703 --> 00:45:07,371
- You want to give it a shot?
- Go for it!

1134
00:45:07,372 --> 00:45:10,640
- I can help if you want.
- I actually love browsing places to stay.

1135
00:45:11,145 --> 00:45:12,576
- It's kind of my hobby.
- Go on, girl.

1136
00:45:12,577 --> 00:45:13,677
(Feeling confident)

1137
00:45:14,045 --> 00:45:16,980
Plus, Won Ji shared her golden rule
for picking accommodations.

1138
00:45:16,981 --> 00:45:17,748
What's the secret?

1139
00:45:17,949 --> 00:45:21,050
She said white sheets are everything.

1140
00:45:21,051 --> 00:45:23,086
Crisp, all-white bedding is
the only way to go.

1141
00:45:23,221 --> 00:45:26,356
If the sheets have loud floral prints
or busy patterns,

1142
00:45:26,691 --> 00:45:28,625
there's a good chance
they're hiding something.

1143
00:45:30,094 --> 00:45:32,762
(Scrolling through options)

1144
00:45:32,763 --> 00:45:33,996
Oh, this one looks promising!

1145
00:45:35,009 --> 00:45:35,808
What do you think of this?

1146
00:45:35,833 --> 00:45:36,933
The view is stunning!

1147
00:45:38,670 --> 00:45:40,993
- This is the one, hands down.
- It looks like Europe.

1148
00:45:40,994 --> 00:45:42,164
(Look what I tracked down)

1149
00:45:42,189 --> 00:45:43,592
- Definitely!
- I really love this!

1150
00:45:43,738 --> 00:45:44,608
Right?

1151
00:45:44,775 --> 00:45:46,142
- For real?
- Seriously?

1152
00:45:46,410 --> 00:45:47,143
Looks great to me!

1153
00:45:47,144 --> 00:45:49,545
You're a quick learner!

1154
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:50,580
Super fast!

1155
00:45:50,748 --> 00:45:52,216
You track down spots in no time!

1156
00:45:53,217 --> 00:45:55,685
Locked it in.
This is where we're crashing!

1157
00:45:55,686 --> 00:45:56,686
(Booking confirmed)

1158
00:45:56,687 --> 00:45:58,021
That meal was so satisfying!

1159
00:45:58,022 --> 00:45:58,822
Seriously hit the spot.

1160
00:45:59,223 --> 00:46:02,392
(Spent 740,000 rupiah
from the Day 10 group fund)

1161
00:46:03,066 --> 00:46:07,003
(Heading back to the car)

1162
00:46:10,101 --> 00:46:12,069
All right, everyone, we're...

1163
00:46:12,270 --> 00:46:13,036
Yes!

1164
00:46:13,204 --> 00:46:14,304
Back on the road!

1165
00:46:14,305 --> 00:46:16,707
We're heading straight to our place
in Cemoro Lawang, right?

1166
00:46:16,708 --> 00:46:17,541
Yes.

1167
00:46:17,909 --> 00:46:19,443
I hear it's quite a trek from here.

1168
00:46:19,911 --> 00:46:22,111
It'll take about three and a half hours.

1169
00:46:22,112 --> 00:46:23,880
Indonesia is ridiculously massive.

1170
00:46:23,881 --> 00:46:25,481
It really is huge.

1171
00:46:25,482 --> 00:46:26,416
Totally.

1172
00:46:27,185 --> 00:46:28,285
I feel so refreshed!

1173
00:46:28,286 --> 00:46:31,731
(A three-and-a-half-hour drive
to their lodging)

1174
00:46:31,756 --> 00:46:33,056
I feel amazing!

1175
00:46:33,257 --> 00:46:35,592
I'm rocking Sian's whole look right now.

1176
00:46:35,593 --> 00:46:37,460
I saw you walking from afar earlier,

1177
00:46:37,461 --> 00:46:39,329
and I was thinking,
"Wow, that outfit is so cute!"

1178
00:46:40,398 --> 00:46:41,631
And it turned out to be your own clothes?

1179
00:46:41,632 --> 00:46:42,733
Yes, straight from my suitcase!

1180
00:46:42,933 --> 00:46:45,969
(Once again deeply impressed
by her own styling)

1181
00:46:46,237 --> 00:46:48,638
I guess that means
I look pretty great in it too!

1182
00:46:48,773 --> 00:46:50,306
"I guess that means
I look pretty great, too."

1183
00:46:50,307 --> 00:46:52,041
"I must look pretty cute in it, then."

1184
00:46:52,910 --> 00:46:55,211
Now we're sharing
our entire wardrobe, it's the best!

1185
00:46:55,479 --> 00:46:57,880
We went from sharing one suitcase
to sharing all our clothes.

1186
00:46:57,881 --> 00:47:00,783
(Only ten days into the trip)

1187
00:47:00,784 --> 00:47:03,519
Won Ji and I even shared a shower!

1188
00:47:03,520 --> 00:47:05,421
Yeah, we share literally everything now.

1189
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:07,090
You guys showered together?

1190
00:47:07,458 --> 00:47:11,418
- No, I meant we shared our toiletries!
- We're not that close yet.

1191
00:47:11,419 --> 00:47:13,129
(Not quite at the showering-together stage
yet.)

1192
00:47:15,032 --> 00:47:17,767
How was Tumpak Sewu for everyone today?

1193
00:47:17,768 --> 00:47:20,603
- Tumpak Sewu...
- Tumpak Sewu Waterfall.

1194
00:47:20,905 --> 00:47:22,739
You truly have to experience it in person.

1195
00:47:22,740 --> 00:47:25,877
I saw so many photos online
while researching it.

1196
00:47:25,878 --> 00:47:27,310
- Before we got here?
- She really did.

1197
00:47:27,311 --> 00:47:31,481
Photos don't even begin to do it justice.

1198
00:47:31,482 --> 00:47:33,283
How does nature...

1199
00:47:33,751 --> 00:47:36,986
even craft something like that?

1200
00:47:36,987 --> 00:47:40,924
The water pours down
in this massive cylinder,

1201
00:47:41,292 --> 00:47:43,059
and hiking right into the middle
of it was magical.

1202
00:47:43,394 --> 00:47:45,261
There was even a rainbow suspended
in the mist!

1203
00:47:46,297 --> 00:47:49,699
It felt like getting pulled
into another realm.

1204
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:52,936
Every single day here makes me
realize how tiny I am.

1205
00:47:53,871 --> 00:47:55,738
Nature really puts you in your place.

1206
00:47:56,540 --> 00:47:58,304
- Hey, don't feel small!
- Never feel small!

1207
00:47:58,305 --> 00:47:59,642
Your presence is huge!

1208
00:48:00,177 --> 00:48:02,445
(Don't shrink away,
not even by a single gram.)

1209
00:48:02,446 --> 00:48:06,182
Nature completely recharged my soul today.

1210
00:48:06,484 --> 00:48:07,918
I feel so rejuvenated.

1211
00:48:07,919 --> 00:48:08,885
- Really?
- Absolutely.

1212
00:48:08,886 --> 00:48:11,655
- I'm bouncing back!
- The second we climbed back up,

1213
00:48:12,056 --> 00:48:14,457
her whole vibe completely flipped.

1214
00:48:14,458 --> 00:48:16,493
Did you see Harimu's pose
on the rocks earlier?

1215
00:48:16,560 --> 00:48:18,828
That was the exact moment
my soul re-entered my body.

1216
00:48:18,829 --> 00:48:20,062
(A scorpion pose powered by Tumpak Sewu)

1217
00:48:20,164 --> 00:48:22,098
- Her bounce-back game is unreal.
- I know, right?

1218
00:48:22,099 --> 00:48:23,800
My recovery rate is legendary!

1219
00:48:23,801 --> 00:48:25,405
- You mean resilience.
- Resilience.

1220
00:48:29,173 --> 00:48:32,208
- Maybe I'm still a little delirious.
- Either way, you're back on your feet!

1221
00:48:32,209 --> 00:48:33,576
My stamina has definitely leveled up.

1222
00:48:34,312 --> 00:48:35,512
I honestly think it has.

1223
00:48:35,647 --> 00:48:36,981
When we tackled those stairs...

1224
00:48:37,114 --> 00:48:38,548
Your endurance is seriously impressive.

1225
00:48:39,950 --> 00:48:41,083
You powered through
without taking a single break!

1226
00:48:41,084 --> 00:48:42,385
Yes, I paced us the whole way.

1227
00:48:42,386 --> 00:48:43,486
That's why none of us burnt out.

1228
00:48:43,721 --> 00:48:45,321
Slow and steady was the way to go.

1229
00:48:47,158 --> 00:48:48,625
I hope you liked it.

1230
00:48:49,960 --> 00:48:52,194
Whoa, look at that peak on the left!

1231
00:48:52,630 --> 00:48:54,531
- Is that a mountain?
- Yes!

1232
00:48:54,532 --> 00:48:55,699
Is that really a mountain?

1233
00:48:55,966 --> 00:48:58,234
Look at it now! Why is it so colossal?

1234
00:48:58,436 --> 00:48:59,603
That has to be a volcano.

1235
00:49:00,905 --> 00:49:03,073
You can see smoke billowing right
out of the peak!

1236
00:49:03,074 --> 00:49:04,307
It's an active volcano!

1237
00:49:04,308 --> 00:49:06,877
(Billowing)

1238
00:49:09,747 --> 00:49:12,015
It's enormous.
I've never seen anything like that!

1239
00:49:14,118 --> 00:49:15,618
I'm pretty sure that's Mount Semeru.

1240
00:49:15,631 --> 00:49:18,031
(Mount Semeru is an active volcano
on Java.)

1241
00:49:18,056 --> 00:49:20,790
Indonesia really is full of volcanoes.

1242
00:49:20,791 --> 00:49:22,592
(The headwaters of Tumpak Sewu Waterfall)

1243
00:49:22,927 --> 00:49:25,394
They say you can see that volcano
right from our village, too.

1244
00:49:25,529 --> 00:49:26,892
And we're driving even closer to it now.

1245
00:49:26,893 --> 00:49:28,631
This is mind-blowing.

1246
00:49:28,799 --> 00:49:30,399
It's gigantic.

1247
00:49:30,835 --> 00:49:32,702
Just how massive is it gonna look
once we get there?

1248
00:49:32,903 --> 00:49:34,470
Straight out of Jurassic Park!

1249
00:49:36,440 --> 00:49:40,910
(Giddy with excitement
for their next stop)

1250
00:49:42,380 --> 00:49:46,049
- This place is just...
- We've driven up so high!

1251
00:49:47,785 --> 00:49:48,752
Look at that drop-off!

1252
00:49:50,588 --> 00:49:52,622
We've been winding uphill
for quite a while now.

1253
00:49:53,258 --> 00:49:54,357
While we've been driving?

1254
00:49:54,358 --> 00:49:55,491
(Winding ever higher up
the mountain roads)

1255
00:49:55,492 --> 00:49:58,928
The scenery on the drive up
has been breathtaking.

1256
00:50:00,881 --> 00:50:01,832
Oh, my!

1257
00:50:02,566 --> 00:50:04,435
It's like "La La Land."

1258
00:50:05,514 --> 00:50:07,771
It looks surreal!

1259
00:50:08,607 --> 00:50:10,607
It's like a movie scene.

1260
00:50:12,543 --> 00:50:15,279
Like a car commercial.

1261
00:50:15,292 --> 00:50:16,480
The curve?

1262
00:50:18,015 --> 00:50:20,618
What is that? Is that like a rest stop?

1263
00:50:20,844 --> 00:50:23,487
- Over there.
- Is that a restaurant?

1264
00:50:23,888 --> 00:50:24,989
Let's stop by.

1265
00:50:25,256 --> 00:50:26,924
Can we stop over here?

1266
00:50:27,057 --> 00:50:29,627
Thank you!

1267
00:50:33,277 --> 00:50:35,866
Awesome! This is great.

1268
00:50:35,867 --> 00:50:37,201
I'm glad we're stopping by.

1269
00:50:37,261 --> 00:50:38,702
Just sitting there would be nice too.

1270
00:50:38,714 --> 00:50:39,570
My goodness.

1271
00:50:40,761 --> 00:50:43,140
Can we sit there?

1272
00:50:43,141 --> 00:50:44,408
Thank you.

1273
00:50:45,075 --> 00:50:47,411
- Amazing!
- Seriously.

1274
00:50:47,412 --> 00:50:49,242
(Entering the rest stop)

1275
00:50:51,015 --> 00:50:52,316
Stunning!

1276
00:50:55,109 --> 00:50:57,109
It looks so beautiful.

1277
00:50:57,781 --> 00:51:00,024
- It's really cool.
- The view is so nice.

1278
00:51:00,524 --> 00:51:02,524
That's insane.

1279
00:51:04,242 --> 00:51:05,663
Look at those clouds.

1280
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:08,632
It's really cool.

1281
00:51:09,287 --> 00:51:10,901
This is unreal.

1282
00:51:10,902 --> 00:51:12,173
(Picturesque)

1283
00:51:12,174 --> 00:51:13,571
I can't believe it.

1284
00:51:13,572 --> 00:51:15,533
- Unbelievable!
- Unbelievable!

1285
00:51:18,172 --> 00:51:21,478
If it were clearer,
we could see Lotte Tower.

1286
00:51:23,837 --> 00:51:25,015
What did she say?

1287
00:51:25,016 --> 00:51:26,750
If the sky were clearer,
she'd be able to see Lotte Tower.

1288
00:51:27,384 --> 00:51:30,387
You know how the tower is visible
from anywhere on a clear day?

1289
00:51:31,017 --> 00:51:32,590
- What?
- When the weather is clear.

1290
00:51:33,257 --> 00:51:35,125
- Seriously.
- She's lost her mind.

1291
00:51:35,126 --> 00:51:36,927
Come here.

1292
00:51:38,044 --> 00:51:40,764
- Shall we get some drinks?
- That's a good idea.

1293
00:51:41,332 --> 00:51:42,766
Four hot coffees.

1294
00:51:42,832 --> 00:51:43,867
Yes, please.

1295
00:51:45,569 --> 00:51:46,437
Oh, dear.

1296
00:51:46,870 --> 00:51:49,672
It's so vast,

1297
00:51:49,732 --> 00:51:51,342
I can't even tell how big it is.

1298
00:51:53,211 --> 00:51:54,211
There's...

1299
00:51:54,212 --> 00:51:57,931
something over there
that looks like a mosque.

1300
00:51:57,932 --> 00:51:58,882
Where?

1301
00:51:59,183 --> 00:52:00,551
That's so tiny.

1302
00:52:00,692 --> 00:52:02,753
- Is that it?
- It's so small.

1303
00:52:03,354 --> 00:52:07,091
- It looks like a little toy.
- It looks miniature.

1304
00:52:07,145 --> 00:52:09,393
I can't believe there's a rest stop...

1305
00:52:09,618 --> 00:52:11,729
- all the way out here.
- So good.

1306
00:52:12,096 --> 00:52:14,531
- This is such a vibe.
- It really is.

1307
00:52:14,532 --> 00:52:16,366
(They stumbled upon a cool spot.)

1308
00:52:20,172 --> 00:52:22,072
(Their drinks are served.)

1309
00:52:22,579 --> 00:52:24,579
It looks nice. They put lids on the cups.

1310
00:52:25,945 --> 00:52:26,977
That's cute.

1311
00:52:28,685 --> 00:52:30,848
It smells like chocolate.

1312
00:52:30,849 --> 00:52:31,931
(Sniffing)

1313
00:52:31,932 --> 00:52:33,517
- Isn't it hot chocolate?
- It smells like chocolate.

1314
00:52:33,892 --> 00:52:35,965
(Sipping)

1315
00:52:36,520 --> 00:52:37,554
It's good.

1316
00:52:38,858 --> 00:52:40,924
It tastes like chocolate and coffee.

1317
00:52:41,358 --> 00:52:42,525
Is it mocha?

1318
00:52:43,327 --> 00:52:44,328
(Surprised)

1319
00:52:45,338 --> 00:52:46,330
What is this?

1320
00:52:46,485 --> 00:52:48,599
- It's so nice.
- It's delicious!

1321
00:52:49,283 --> 00:52:50,367
It's really good.

1322
00:52:51,192 --> 00:52:52,436
An unexpected find!

1323
00:52:52,703 --> 00:52:53,837
Excuse me.

1324
00:52:54,471 --> 00:52:55,539
What is this?

1325
00:52:56,140 --> 00:52:57,474
- Mocha?
- That's it.

1326
00:52:59,637 --> 00:53:00,477
Correct.

1327
00:53:00,490 --> 00:53:01,812
That's the one!

1328
00:53:03,624 --> 00:53:04,948
It's good.

1329
00:53:05,097 --> 00:53:07,117
It's really good.
I have to take a picture.

1330
00:53:07,977 --> 00:53:10,754
I'm going to miss this
once I'm back in Korea.

1331
00:53:11,230 --> 00:53:13,924
This rest stop has an amazing view.

1332
00:53:14,725 --> 00:53:16,760
Harimu found a good spot.

1333
00:53:17,528 --> 00:53:18,629
Thanks.

1334
00:53:19,575 --> 00:53:20,774
(They don't forget to take a picture.)

1335
00:53:20,775 --> 00:53:21,965
Should I face this way?

1336
00:53:23,362 --> 00:53:25,235
(Now they pose naturally.)

1337
00:53:26,547 --> 00:53:29,207
(Making more and more memories together)

1338
00:53:29,940 --> 00:53:32,743
Tomorrow is our last day.

1339
00:53:32,767 --> 00:53:34,144
Already!

1340
00:53:35,512 --> 00:53:37,981
Time felt slow, but it went by so fast.

1341
00:53:38,348 --> 00:53:40,117
I felt like it flew by.

1342
00:53:40,318 --> 00:53:41,552
It flew by.

1343
00:53:42,405 --> 00:53:43,786
(Staring)

1344
00:53:43,787 --> 00:53:45,122
Why do you look so pretty today?

1345
00:53:45,456 --> 00:53:47,891
Because I haven't worn my hair down
in a while.

1346
00:53:48,392 --> 00:53:50,392
She blow-dried her hair today.

1347
00:53:50,393 --> 00:53:53,286
All the puffiness in my face is gone...

1348
00:53:53,287 --> 00:53:54,880
because I got everything out.

1349
00:53:55,013 --> 00:53:57,868
I completely emptied out my entire system.

1350
00:53:59,406 --> 00:54:01,338
She emptied herself out.

1351
00:54:01,387 --> 00:54:02,406
Right.

1352
00:54:03,407 --> 00:54:05,442
You're immune now.

1353
00:54:05,809 --> 00:54:07,520
You won't get sick again.

1354
00:54:09,241 --> 00:54:12,101
(There she goes again,
celebrating the upgrade.)

1355
00:54:13,428 --> 00:54:14,473
(Wiping her nose)

1356
00:54:14,474 --> 00:54:16,174
(Spinning her fingers)

1357
00:54:16,734 --> 00:54:19,214
(Now she's used to it.)

1358
00:54:19,554 --> 00:54:23,248
(The four of them have grown close.)

1359
00:54:24,021 --> 00:54:26,597
Mount Bromo.

1360
00:54:27,280 --> 00:54:29,007
(Looking up their next destination)

1361
00:54:29,833 --> 00:54:32,736
It's one of the best sunrise spots.

1362
00:54:32,737 --> 00:54:35,672
- Really?
- A sunrise tour.

1363
00:54:37,490 --> 00:54:39,224
(Cemoro Lawang, Indonesia)

1364
00:54:40,364 --> 00:54:42,804
(A village sitting about 2,200 meters
above sea level)

1365
00:54:46,490 --> 00:54:49,877
(A massive volcano is
right in front of it.)

1366
00:54:50,537 --> 00:54:57,217
(Golden sunrise and the sea of clouds
make a breathtaking view.)

1367
00:55:01,057 --> 00:55:04,237
(You can get up close
to an active volcano...)

1368
00:55:05,257 --> 00:55:07,857
(on the Mount Bromo trek.)

1369
00:55:08,890 --> 00:55:15,310
(You can feel the beauty of nature...)

1370
00:55:15,690 --> 00:55:18,843
(on Abra-ca-Empty's fourth type
of terrain.)

1371
00:55:18,844 --> 00:55:21,550
(Cemoro Lawang,
where our Mount Bromo tour begins)

1372
00:55:21,643 --> 00:55:23,086
We have to see the sunrise.

1373
00:55:23,223 --> 00:55:24,087
Seriously.

1374
00:55:24,203 --> 00:55:27,224
- Didn't Fin mention King Kong Hill?
- Right.

1375
00:55:27,363 --> 00:55:29,363
He said we should check out
King Kong Hill.

1376
00:55:30,227 --> 00:55:34,773
So, apparently, there's a Jeep photo spot.

1377
00:55:34,774 --> 00:55:36,967
- You climb on it and take pictures.
- You climb onto a Jeep.

1378
00:55:36,968 --> 00:55:38,101
That's hip!

1379
00:55:38,102 --> 00:55:40,204
- We should dress up!
- We should look good!

1380
00:55:40,361 --> 00:55:43,068
I just want to wear a simple top
and leggings.

1381
00:55:43,069 --> 00:55:44,508
I like that.

1382
00:55:44,896 --> 00:55:46,243
That would look good.

1383
00:55:46,244 --> 00:55:47,529
(Planning tomorrow's outfit)

1384
00:55:47,809 --> 00:55:52,316
It seems like they have a tour here too.

1385
00:55:52,429 --> 00:55:55,080
Shall we ask the owner
of our lodging later?

1386
00:55:55,100 --> 00:55:57,721
They must know a lot about it
since they work...

1387
00:55:57,722 --> 00:56:00,958
- in the hospitality business.
- There are so many tours.

1388
00:56:00,987 --> 00:56:02,073
Good point.

1389
00:56:02,233 --> 00:56:05,495
- Now you're a travel expert.
- Of course.

1390
00:56:05,513 --> 00:56:07,197
(What?)

1391
00:56:07,420 --> 00:56:09,066
(Putting on a fake accent)

1392
00:56:09,067 --> 00:56:10,667
- You bet!
- What do you think...

1393
00:56:10,668 --> 00:56:12,936
when someone fakes a dialect?

1394
00:56:13,266 --> 00:56:15,572
- I heard some people hate it.
- I don't hate it,

1395
00:56:15,612 --> 00:56:16,846
but it stuns me.

1396
00:56:16,847 --> 00:56:18,319
Hey, I saw this!

1397
00:56:18,320 --> 00:56:20,944
- Your accent lesson!
- Right.

1398
00:56:20,945 --> 00:56:21,979
How do you speak?

1399
00:56:21,980 --> 00:56:23,912
- Can you do your Busan accent?
- We talk like this.

1400
00:56:24,281 --> 00:56:25,913
Don't imitate our accent.

1401
00:56:26,026 --> 00:56:27,317
(Impactful)

1402
00:56:27,318 --> 00:56:29,633
- You really sound like you're from Busan.
- I do?

1403
00:56:30,387 --> 00:56:33,156
- "Don't imitate our accent."
- I'm from Busan.

1404
00:56:33,457 --> 00:56:35,457
You can really hear the Busan accent.

1405
00:56:35,792 --> 00:56:38,098
Hey, look here.

1406
00:56:38,362 --> 00:56:40,663
Hey, look here.

1407
00:56:41,519 --> 00:56:43,267
Go catch some fish.

1408
00:56:43,910 --> 00:56:45,469
Fillet some sashimi.

1409
00:56:46,090 --> 00:56:47,004
I'm sorry.

1410
00:56:47,005 --> 00:56:48,872
- That's crazy.
- That's crazy.

1411
00:56:48,905 --> 00:56:50,407
- "Fillet some sashimi."
- My goodness.

1412
00:56:50,478 --> 00:56:52,576
What do you think about this?

1413
00:56:52,876 --> 00:56:54,511
"I like you!"

1414
00:56:55,065 --> 00:56:56,847
(Imitating an accent she heard
in the media)

1415
00:56:56,848 --> 00:56:57,741
An accent like that?

1416
00:56:57,801 --> 00:56:59,249
Do you guys really say that?

1417
00:56:59,513 --> 00:57:01,121
No way.

1418
00:57:01,122 --> 00:57:03,020
- How do you guys confess, then?
- I don't know.

1419
00:57:03,021 --> 00:57:04,201
It depends.

1420
00:57:04,221 --> 00:57:06,790
Won Ji, try confessing your feelings.

1421
00:57:06,791 --> 00:57:09,526
How would you say,
"Do you want to be my girlfriend?"

1422
00:57:09,584 --> 00:57:11,762
Hey, be my girlfriend!

1423
00:57:11,951 --> 00:57:13,563
You're lying.

1424
00:57:13,791 --> 00:57:15,165
Hey!

1425
00:57:15,666 --> 00:57:16,800
Let's date.

1426
00:57:16,872 --> 00:57:18,552
"Let's date."

1427
00:57:18,553 --> 00:57:20,504
- That sounds like authentic Busan.
- Really?

1428
00:57:20,505 --> 00:57:22,773
I think younger people might sound softer.

1429
00:57:23,298 --> 00:57:24,741
Come to my place with me.

1430
00:57:25,609 --> 00:57:28,612
Even I can tell
Sian is pretty bad at this.

1431
00:57:32,783 --> 00:57:34,584
There's something awkward about it.

1432
00:57:34,585 --> 00:57:36,687
No. I'm not bad.

1433
00:57:36,882 --> 00:57:39,289
- That wasn't that bad.
- I sound good.

1434
00:57:39,496 --> 00:57:43,193
If you make a wish at this crater,
it'll come true.

1435
00:57:43,276 --> 00:57:44,289
- Is that so?
- Really?

1436
00:57:44,322 --> 00:57:46,563
What do you want to wish for?

1437
00:57:47,390 --> 00:57:49,540
I hope Abra-ca-Empty blows up.

1438
00:57:49,541 --> 00:57:50,767
- Me too.
- Abra-ca-Empty.

1439
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:52,836
I hope Abra-ca-Empty becomes
a huge success...

1440
00:57:52,837 --> 00:57:55,614
and we all end up living
in mansions in LA.

1441
00:57:55,667 --> 00:57:57,240
Is that possible?

1442
00:57:57,347 --> 00:57:58,909
I hope it gets that big.

1443
00:57:58,980 --> 00:58:01,778
- It blows up enough for that.
- How big does it have to get?

1444
00:58:01,853 --> 00:58:04,120
I hope it becomes an absurdly huge hit.

1445
00:58:04,554 --> 00:58:09,027
I hope it gets insanely popular.

1446
00:58:09,127 --> 00:58:10,988
I want to move next to Justin Bieber.

1447
00:58:10,989 --> 00:58:12,227
- I like that.
- Really?

1448
00:58:12,228 --> 00:58:14,324
- For me, next door to Kim Kardashian.
- I like that!

1449
00:58:14,325 --> 00:58:15,774
We'll be in the same neighborhood.

1450
00:58:15,815 --> 00:58:17,815
- No, we won't.
- I'm sorry.

1451
00:58:18,996 --> 00:58:20,263
I apologize.

1452
00:58:20,264 --> 00:58:22,021
(Even if their wishes come true,
they won't be neighbors.)

1453
00:58:22,622 --> 00:58:26,103
Let's make our show a big hit
and move to LA.

1454
00:58:26,162 --> 00:58:27,316
- Okay!
- Mansions in LA!

1455
00:58:27,317 --> 00:58:29,940
- Let's go!
- That's going to be my wish.

1456
00:58:30,616 --> 00:58:32,376
Let's take a video and leave.

1457
00:58:32,675 --> 00:58:33,777
I have an idea.

1458
00:58:34,478 --> 00:58:36,613
We do this in three.

1459
00:58:37,187 --> 00:58:38,469
- You know what I mean.
- Yes.

1460
00:58:38,470 --> 00:58:39,983
- Lift your cups.
- Okay.

1461
00:58:39,984 --> 00:58:41,864
(I got it!)

1462
00:58:41,944 --> 00:58:45,284
Let's kneel down
and sit in a line over there.

1463
00:58:45,285 --> 00:58:46,289
Okay.

1464
00:58:46,797 --> 00:58:49,359
Okay. Practice. In 1, 2, 3.

1465
00:58:49,360 --> 00:58:50,660
(Gasping)

1466
00:58:52,407 --> 00:58:55,332
I don't think it's going to look good.
Let's see.

1467
00:58:55,966 --> 00:58:57,966
- Look.
- Won Ji, you took a picture.

1468
00:58:57,967 --> 00:58:59,136
Is that a picture?

1469
00:58:59,593 --> 00:59:01,260
- Wait.
- Hey.

1470
00:59:01,938 --> 00:59:03,407
Here we go.

1471
00:59:03,740 --> 00:59:05,876
In 1, 2, 3.

1472
00:59:10,315 --> 00:59:11,848
- It's pretty good, right?
- It's not bad.

1473
00:59:12,115 --> 00:59:13,216
- Pass!
- Okay.

1474
00:59:13,217 --> 00:59:15,318
Ms. Influencer gave me a pass.

1475
00:59:15,319 --> 00:59:16,119
Pass!

1476
00:59:17,668 --> 00:59:19,322
It's easier to get in through the trunk.

1477
00:59:19,323 --> 00:59:22,017
(Getting back in the car)

1478
00:59:22,950 --> 00:59:24,194
Thank you.

1479
00:59:25,663 --> 00:59:29,589
(Back on the road to Cemoro Lawang)

1480
00:59:29,866 --> 00:59:31,506
Is that volcanic ash too?

1481
00:59:31,507 --> 00:59:33,210
- You're right!
- This is all volcanic ash.

1482
00:59:33,211 --> 00:59:34,137
Right?

1483
00:59:35,439 --> 00:59:36,740
It's a world of volcanic ash!

1484
00:59:36,871 --> 00:59:39,691
It looked so black from up there.
I thought it was volcanic ash.

1485
00:59:39,692 --> 00:59:41,902
The stuff the excavator was digging up
earlier must be volcanic ash too.

1486
00:59:41,903 --> 00:59:42,809
I guess so.

1487
00:59:42,905 --> 00:59:45,849
Do you think they make
volcanic ash face masks out of that?

1488
00:59:46,392 --> 00:59:47,625
Volcanic ash face masks?

1489
00:59:47,658 --> 00:59:48,685
What is a volcanic ash face mask?

1490
00:59:48,725 --> 00:59:49,653
Isn't that a thing?

1491
00:59:50,445 --> 00:59:52,155
You're talking...

1492
00:59:52,358 --> 00:59:55,025
about volcanic rock face masks.

1493
00:59:55,050 --> 00:59:56,391
- Volcanic rocks?
- Volcanic rocks?

1494
00:59:57,661 --> 00:59:59,469
If you cover your face
with volcanic ash...

1495
00:59:59,596 --> 01:00:01,664
I think it's kind of inspired by it.

1496
01:00:01,665 --> 01:00:03,299
I don't think it actually contains any.

1497
01:00:03,300 --> 01:00:04,924
Our beauty expert!

1498
01:00:04,925 --> 01:00:09,538
- Beauty!
- Beauty queen!

1499
01:00:09,940 --> 01:00:11,407
Our beauty queen!

1500
01:00:11,408 --> 01:00:12,375
Queen.

1501
01:00:13,010 --> 01:00:14,877
Volcanic ash on your face.

1502
01:00:16,079 --> 01:00:18,614
We can really talk forever
about absolutely nothing.

1503
01:00:18,615 --> 01:00:20,983
- Yeah.
- I love it.

1504
01:00:20,984 --> 01:00:21,952
"I love it."

1505
01:00:22,047 --> 01:00:23,045
I love talking about...

1506
01:00:23,046 --> 01:00:24,146
absolutely nothing.

1507
01:00:24,154 --> 01:00:27,490
You really love these things, don't you?

1508
01:00:27,626 --> 01:00:29,535
But it's true.

1509
01:00:29,536 --> 01:00:31,327
(As they chat away,
a small village comes into view.)

1510
01:00:31,328 --> 01:00:32,394
You're good.

1511
01:00:33,196 --> 01:00:35,230
Is it kind of hazy here
because of the volcanic ash?

1512
01:00:36,299 --> 01:00:38,399
- Could be.
- The wind could've carried it.

1513
01:00:38,400 --> 01:00:40,502
Probably,
since smoke comes out constantly.

1514
01:00:41,038 --> 01:00:44,140
And you can see the smoke too.

1515
01:00:44,141 --> 01:00:45,308
(A village
beside a smoking active volcano)

1516
01:00:45,776 --> 01:00:48,044
The ash keeps falling,

1517
01:00:48,412 --> 01:00:50,346
so they're sweeping
in front of their homes.

1518
01:00:50,914 --> 01:00:52,314
Really?

1519
01:00:52,315 --> 01:00:53,249
Look at all the black stuff.

1520
01:00:53,250 --> 01:00:55,051
There's volcanic ash everywhere.

1521
01:00:55,052 --> 01:00:56,653
There's so much.

1522
01:00:56,654 --> 01:00:59,054
- Even the floors.
- It's covered in black.

1523
01:00:59,456 --> 01:01:01,657
My slippers suddenly feel all gritty.

1524
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:02,691
Like there's sand in them.

1525
01:01:02,692 --> 01:01:03,626
For some reason.

1526
01:01:03,627 --> 01:01:05,127
- Just feels like it.
- For some reason.

1527
01:01:05,563 --> 01:01:07,730
There are a lot of big trucks
going back and forth.

1528
01:01:08,498 --> 01:01:10,432
They're loaded with volcanic ash.

1529
01:01:11,034 --> 01:01:13,168
All these huge trucks...

1530
01:01:13,169 --> 01:01:14,803
are loaded with volcanic ash.

1531
01:01:15,105 --> 01:01:16,305
Maybe...

1532
01:01:16,306 --> 01:01:19,442
they make something out of it?

1533
01:01:20,243 --> 01:01:22,044
They're taking the volcanic ash!

1534
01:01:22,045 --> 01:01:23,212
Yeah.

1535
01:01:23,213 --> 01:01:24,546
They're spraying a lot of water.

1536
01:01:24,547 --> 01:01:26,481
They're cleaning the trucks too.

1537
01:01:27,050 --> 01:01:29,485
That truck was covered in ash just now.

1538
01:01:29,920 --> 01:01:33,155
Doesn't it stick to a battery
if you hold one up to it?

1539
01:01:33,156 --> 01:01:34,490
Earlier,

1540
01:01:34,491 --> 01:01:36,525
Sian dropped her phone.

1541
01:01:36,526 --> 01:01:37,827
When she picked it up,

1542
01:01:37,828 --> 01:01:39,395
- there was black stuff on the back.
- That's right.

1543
01:01:40,397 --> 01:01:42,899
- That must've been the ash.
- On the magnetic part!

1544
01:01:42,900 --> 01:01:43,732
That's right.

1545
01:01:43,733 --> 01:01:44,733
(Interesting)

1546
01:01:45,068 --> 01:01:46,573
This world is full of fun.

1547
01:01:47,437 --> 01:01:49,805
This place is already so much fun.

1548
01:01:50,507 --> 01:01:52,908
I've never been this close
to an active volcano before.

1549
01:01:54,411 --> 01:01:57,747
It's so cool that
there's actual volcanic ash here.

1550
01:01:57,748 --> 01:02:00,182
- Yeah.
- There are so many black mountains.

1551
01:02:00,183 --> 01:02:01,050
(The unfamiliar scenery only adds
to the excitement.)

1552
01:02:01,852 --> 01:02:04,854
- Wait, the sun's already setting?
- I was thinking the same.

1553
01:02:04,855 --> 01:02:06,022
The sun's down already.

1554
01:02:07,324 --> 01:02:08,257
What time is it?

1555
01:02:08,692 --> 01:02:09,859
It's around 5 p.m.

1556
01:02:09,860 --> 01:02:11,727
It's 10 to 5.

1557
01:02:12,162 --> 01:02:14,930
Do we have 2 to 3 more hours to go?

1558
01:02:14,931 --> 01:02:16,265
Two and a half, I think.

1559
01:02:16,367 --> 01:02:17,366
There's still a lot left.

1560
01:02:19,469 --> 01:02:20,836
I'm so excited to see the volcano.

1561
01:02:21,238 --> 01:02:22,104
Me too.

1562
01:02:22,472 --> 01:02:24,072
I wonder how incredible it'll be.

1563
01:02:24,073 --> 01:02:25,541
- Indeed.
- The scenery...

1564
01:02:32,015 --> 01:02:33,382
(Staring)

1565
01:02:33,383 --> 01:02:35,251
Isn't that all volcanic ash?

1566
01:02:35,252 --> 01:02:36,352
Is this it?

1567
01:02:37,787 --> 01:02:38,620
Where?

1568
01:02:38,621 --> 01:02:39,654
- Really?
- This one.

1569
01:02:40,390 --> 01:02:41,590
I think that's volcanic ash.

1570
01:02:41,591 --> 01:02:42,525
(Eyes wide open)

1571
01:02:42,526 --> 01:02:43,392
It is!

1572
01:02:44,027 --> 01:02:46,128
I've never seen anything like this before.

1573
01:02:47,030 --> 01:02:47,930
Wow.

1574
01:02:48,031 --> 01:02:51,399
(Jet-black volcanic ash
stretches out below the bridge.)

1575
01:02:51,400 --> 01:02:53,101
Hello, volcanic ash!

1576
01:02:53,436 --> 01:02:55,738
We're coming for you, volcanic ash!

1577
01:02:55,939 --> 01:02:57,206
Volcano!

1578
01:02:57,307 --> 01:02:58,274
See you soon!

1579
01:02:58,275 --> 01:03:01,577
- I miss you, volcano!
- Wait for me, volcano.

1580
01:03:02,113 --> 01:03:03,846
I can already sense
the volcano's presence.

1581
01:03:03,847 --> 01:03:05,982
- Volcano vibe!
- Totally.

1582
01:03:06,650 --> 01:03:10,853
(On their way to the volcano.
Wonder what will happen.)

1583
01:03:12,689 --> 01:03:15,157
I wanted volcano as my dancer name once.

1584
01:03:15,158 --> 01:03:16,492
- Really?
- Did you?

1585
01:03:16,493 --> 01:03:17,526
No, I'm just joking.

1586
01:03:17,527 --> 01:03:21,397
(With excitement building,
they drive on for a while.)

1587
01:03:22,432 --> 01:03:23,933
It's rest time.

1588
01:03:23,934 --> 01:03:24,867
Rest.

1589
01:03:25,035 --> 01:03:26,635
- Is there a convenience store?
- Yes.

1590
01:03:26,636 --> 01:03:29,138
- Are we going to the convenience store?
- Let's go.

1591
01:03:29,673 --> 01:03:30,806
Let's see what's inside.

1592
01:03:30,807 --> 01:03:31,907
(Checking out the gas station
convenience store)

1593
01:03:31,908 --> 01:03:32,842
Wonder what they have.

1594
01:03:33,443 --> 01:03:35,444
- Shin ramyeon!
- Shin ramyeon!

1595
01:03:35,946 --> 01:03:37,713
Can we cook it?

1596
01:03:37,948 --> 01:03:40,716
I think there's a pot at the hotel.

1597
01:03:41,351 --> 01:03:44,586
A perfect chance to have a ramyeon party.

1598
01:03:44,821 --> 01:03:45,988
Let's take them all.

1599
01:03:45,989 --> 01:03:47,856
Okay! Take them all!

1600
01:03:47,857 --> 01:03:49,291
How many people are there?

1601
01:03:49,292 --> 01:03:51,727
(Buying ramyeon for the crew too.)

1602
01:03:51,728 --> 01:03:52,795
This one's really good!

1603
01:03:52,796 --> 01:03:54,563
- This one?
- Let's buy that too.

1604
01:03:54,564 --> 01:03:55,798
Let's buy these three.

1605
01:03:55,799 --> 01:03:56,632
Awesome.

1606
01:03:56,633 --> 01:03:57,800
(Grabbing one of every
instant noodle on the shelf)

1607
01:03:57,801 --> 01:04:00,335
- Shin ramyeon toowoomba's really good.
- They will make some money today.

1608
01:04:01,738 --> 01:04:02,971
"Hotter than my ex."

1609
01:04:04,874 --> 01:04:06,308
"Hotter than my ex!"

1610
01:04:06,676 --> 01:04:08,710
"Hotter than my ex!"

1611
01:04:09,179 --> 01:04:13,516
(Here she goes. Again.)

1612
01:04:15,218 --> 01:04:17,186
Hotter! Than my ex.

1613
01:04:20,857 --> 01:04:22,958
You okay?
Have we been in the car too long?

1614
01:04:22,959 --> 01:04:24,092
(Swish)

1615
01:04:24,093 --> 01:04:26,628
Have we been in the car too long?

1616
01:04:27,130 --> 01:04:27,930
(Scratching)

1617
01:04:27,931 --> 01:04:28,731
Harimu.

1618
01:04:29,032 --> 01:04:32,168
The truth is, we love shopping.

1619
01:04:32,169 --> 01:04:34,003
That's right.
Shopping makes us happy like this.

1620
01:04:34,271 --> 01:04:35,204
However!

1621
01:04:35,605 --> 01:04:38,173
We've been climbing mountains nonstop.

1622
01:04:38,775 --> 01:04:41,744
- Climbing!
- Mountain after mountain.

1623
01:04:42,312 --> 01:04:43,479
Mountain over mountain.

1624
01:04:43,480 --> 01:04:46,682
- Yeah. Mountain of mountains.
- M.O.M.

1625
01:04:46,917 --> 01:04:48,283
Thank you.

1626
01:04:48,284 --> 01:04:50,085
Thank you!

1627
01:04:50,086 --> 01:04:52,287
Good night.

1628
01:04:53,022 --> 01:04:56,992
(Getting some fresh air for a bit)

1629
01:04:57,460 --> 01:04:59,127
Yeah, let's go!

1630
01:05:00,330 --> 01:05:02,264
I can't believe we bought ramyeon.

1631
01:05:02,265 --> 01:05:04,600
(Off to the hotel again)

1632
01:05:06,803 --> 01:05:11,774
(Cruising down the highway)

1633
01:05:12,542 --> 01:05:13,809
We're almost there.

1634
01:05:14,244 --> 01:05:15,578
Our hotel...

1635
01:05:15,712 --> 01:05:18,247
is near the entrance of the volcano.

1636
01:05:18,248 --> 01:05:19,615
- It's at the entrance.
- Right near it.

1637
01:05:19,950 --> 01:05:22,951
Which means we're going pretty high.

1638
01:05:22,952 --> 01:05:24,353
My ears are popping.

1639
01:05:25,488 --> 01:05:29,058
Which means there's magma
flowing right next to us.

1640
01:05:29,059 --> 01:05:30,493
(They climb higher
along the winding road.)

1641
01:05:31,094 --> 01:05:33,095
It's the place I saw on the street view.

1642
01:05:33,096 --> 01:05:33,929
(They enter a quiet village.)

1643
01:05:33,930 --> 01:05:35,230
It's really cold right now.

1644
01:05:35,565 --> 01:05:37,566
We don't have any winter clothes, though.

1645
01:05:38,768 --> 01:05:40,869
Yeah. It was hot summer just a while ago.

1646
01:05:41,571 --> 01:05:42,971
How can the weather be like this?

1647
01:05:44,040 --> 01:05:46,075
Who knew it'd become this cold?

1648
01:05:46,076 --> 01:05:47,509
I never saw this coming.

1649
01:05:48,011 --> 01:05:49,878
Everyone's wearing puffer jackets.

1650
01:05:49,879 --> 01:05:51,380
They're even wearing beanies.

1651
01:05:51,715 --> 01:05:52,848
It must be really cold.

1652
01:05:53,149 --> 01:05:54,649
How is this possible?

1653
01:05:54,650 --> 01:05:55,684
(Tourists are wearing winter clothes.)

1654
01:05:55,685 --> 01:05:56,751
It's winter all of a sudden?

1655
01:05:58,455 --> 01:06:00,623
- They sell socks.
- Yeah.

1656
01:06:00,990 --> 01:06:02,090
And beanies too.

1657
01:06:02,091 --> 01:06:04,125
(Selling cold weather gear everywhere)

1658
01:06:04,126 --> 01:06:05,927
Okay.

1659
01:06:07,297 --> 01:06:10,399
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1660
01:06:11,034 --> 01:06:12,201
Thank you.

1661
01:06:12,202 --> 01:06:14,003
Let's get out, shall we?

1662
01:06:14,004 --> 01:06:15,304
Don't forget our backpacks.

1663
01:06:15,305 --> 01:06:16,739
(They arrived at the hotel.)

1664
01:06:17,640 --> 01:06:19,608
- Wow, it's cold!
- So cold.

1665
01:06:19,876 --> 01:06:21,076
- It really is cold.
- It's freezing.

1666
01:06:21,077 --> 01:06:23,011
This is so odd.
It feels like early winter.

1667
01:06:23,012 --> 01:06:24,613
I think they sell socks over there.

1668
01:06:24,614 --> 01:06:26,415
I want that beanie.

1669
01:06:26,416 --> 01:06:28,183
Let's at least get those. It's so cold.

1670
01:06:28,619 --> 01:06:30,919
- Let's go check in first.
- Of course.

1671
01:06:30,920 --> 01:06:33,622
This weather's so interesting.

1672
01:06:33,623 --> 01:06:34,456
(Heading to reception to check in)

1673
01:06:35,725 --> 01:06:38,493
Hello. Can we check in now?

1674
01:06:40,363 --> 01:06:42,197
- Please follow me.
- Okay.

1675
01:06:43,467 --> 01:06:44,604
I think we can check in right now.

1676
01:06:45,201 --> 01:06:47,335
Just like that?

1677
01:06:47,537 --> 01:06:49,304
I love it.

1678
01:06:49,305 --> 01:06:50,839
Thank you.

1679
01:06:51,375 --> 01:06:54,543
Can we book the sunrise tour?

1680
01:06:54,544 --> 01:06:55,745
Oh, the Jeep tour?

1681
01:06:55,746 --> 01:06:57,246
- Yes.
- Yes, you can.

1682
01:06:57,247 --> 01:06:59,748
- We'd like to book it.
- Okay.

1683
01:06:59,749 --> 01:07:02,584
Sunrise tour for tomorrow morning, please.

1684
01:07:02,585 --> 01:07:04,586
- Okay, I'll book it for you.
- Okay!

1685
01:07:04,587 --> 01:07:05,821
(One sunrise tour, please!)

1686
01:07:06,022 --> 01:07:07,923
- Thank you.
- The tour will cost...

1687
01:07:08,358 --> 01:07:09,892
Seventy dollars total for four.

1688
01:07:09,893 --> 01:07:11,327
- U.S. dollars?
- Yes.

1689
01:07:11,528 --> 01:07:13,996
- For all of us?
- Yes.

1690
01:07:13,997 --> 01:07:16,432
What time do we leave?

1691
01:07:16,833 --> 01:07:18,934
- Three in the morning.
- Three?

1692
01:07:19,903 --> 01:07:21,770
Wow, that's so early!

1693
01:07:21,771 --> 01:07:23,239
That early?

1694
01:07:23,240 --> 01:07:25,341
We rent out jackets here.

1695
01:07:25,342 --> 01:07:26,175
Okay.

1696
01:07:26,176 --> 01:07:27,676
We don't have jackets.

1697
01:07:27,677 --> 01:07:29,378
We can rent jackets?

1698
01:07:29,779 --> 01:07:31,079
Let's rent jackets.

1699
01:07:31,948 --> 01:07:34,283
How much is it?

1700
01:07:34,484 --> 01:07:35,884
Ten dollars per jacket.

1701
01:07:36,019 --> 01:07:37,086
Okay.

1702
01:07:37,421 --> 01:07:39,255
Forty dollars for four.

1703
01:07:39,256 --> 01:07:40,890
- Okay, got it.
- Great.

1704
01:07:41,290 --> 01:07:43,959
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1705
01:07:43,960 --> 01:07:45,427
Come inside. It's cold.

1706
01:07:45,428 --> 01:07:46,595
(King Kong Hill sunrise tour booked)

1707
01:07:47,230 --> 01:07:48,597
(Finally taking a tour of the room)

1708
01:07:48,598 --> 01:07:49,832
This place is nice.

1709
01:07:50,767 --> 01:07:53,035
Look! We can cook ramyeon over there.

1710
01:07:53,036 --> 01:07:54,269
Yes!

1711
01:07:54,270 --> 01:07:55,270
(A cozy, homestay-style hotel
for travelers)

1712
01:07:56,306 --> 01:07:59,475
(A clean and cozy bedroom)

1713
01:07:59,776 --> 01:08:01,343
I wish we had clothes.

1714
01:08:01,878 --> 01:08:03,245
We don't even have socks.

1715
01:08:03,947 --> 01:08:06,382
Should we go buy some?
I think they sell socks and beanies.

1716
01:08:06,383 --> 01:08:07,449
Yes, please.

1717
01:08:07,784 --> 01:08:08,984
I want a beanie too.

1718
01:08:08,985 --> 01:08:10,853
Good idea. I saw some beanies earlier...

1719
01:08:10,854 --> 01:08:12,855
with "Bromo" written on them.

1720
01:08:12,856 --> 01:08:15,390
Really? That's so our thing.

1721
01:08:15,391 --> 01:08:17,426
It's a perfect souvenir.

1722
01:08:17,427 --> 01:08:19,194
- Totally our thing.
- You know what that is, right?

1723
01:08:19,195 --> 01:08:21,697
"I love Bromo volcano."

1724
01:08:21,698 --> 01:08:22,898
I love it.

1725
01:08:22,899 --> 01:08:25,501
It's 15 degrees Celsius.
I just looked it up.

1726
01:08:25,502 --> 01:08:27,002
Only 15, and it's this cold?

1727
01:08:27,003 --> 01:08:28,670
It feels like it's at least 10.

1728
01:08:28,671 --> 01:08:30,939
Is it because we just came from
somewhere so hot?

1729
01:08:30,940 --> 01:08:31,907
It feels like...

1730
01:08:32,047 --> 01:08:34,849
seven degrees, honestly.

1731
01:08:35,045 --> 01:08:36,511
Minus seven degrees?

1732
01:08:36,512 --> 01:08:38,880
It's colder since we're wearing
short sleeves.

1733
01:08:39,247 --> 01:08:41,349
Let's go grab our suitcase...

1734
01:08:41,350 --> 01:08:42,450
and organize it first.

1735
01:08:42,451 --> 01:08:44,252
- Yeah.
- Let's put more clothes on.

1736
01:08:44,253 --> 01:08:46,287
- It's so cold.
- Okay.

1737
01:08:46,523 --> 01:08:48,090
Wow, it's so cold.

1738
01:08:48,791 --> 01:08:50,403
I think...

1739
01:08:50,404 --> 01:08:55,263
we should buy some
from those people we saw earlier.

1740
01:08:55,465 --> 01:08:58,867
We should buy some socks and pants.

1741
01:08:58,868 --> 01:08:59,802
Not pants.

1742
01:08:59,803 --> 01:09:03,105
There it is! Hats!

1743
01:09:03,106 --> 01:09:05,207
We need hats!

1744
01:09:05,208 --> 01:09:06,252
Look! Wow.

1745
01:09:06,253 --> 01:09:07,409
(Found the hat seller they saw earlier)

1746
01:09:07,577 --> 01:09:09,378
This gray one looks cool.

1747
01:09:09,379 --> 01:09:10,879
(You can tell the hats are super warm.)

1748
01:09:10,880 --> 01:09:11,914
The pink one is pretty too.

1749
01:09:12,382 --> 01:09:13,632
It's a tough choice.

1750
01:09:13,850 --> 01:09:15,918
It's so cold. I'm choosing
between these two.

1751
01:09:16,186 --> 01:09:17,686
- The pink one suits you.
- The pink one's pretty.

1752
01:09:17,687 --> 01:09:18,520
It suits you better.

1753
01:09:18,521 --> 01:09:20,355
Okay, then. I'll buy pink.

1754
01:09:20,790 --> 01:09:23,158
- Brown.
- And this one.

1755
01:09:23,359 --> 01:09:24,759
(How do I look?)

1756
01:09:24,760 --> 01:09:27,362
You look so cute. Look at the tip!

1757
01:09:27,363 --> 01:09:28,163
(Maybe it's slightly big.)

1758
01:09:28,164 --> 01:09:29,164
How much is it?

1759
01:09:29,165 --> 01:09:30,432
A hundred thousand rupiah.

1760
01:09:30,767 --> 01:09:32,301
- It's 100,000 rupiah?
- It's 100,000?

1761
01:09:32,302 --> 01:09:33,102
(Around 8.50 dollars)

1762
01:09:33,236 --> 01:09:35,571
- All right, then.
- Go ahead.

1763
01:09:35,572 --> 01:09:36,805
Four, please.

1764
01:09:37,273 --> 01:09:38,306
We're paying with the group fund.

1765
01:09:38,307 --> 01:09:39,674
Sure.

1766
01:09:42,612 --> 01:09:44,847
(Dancing in her own little world)

1767
01:09:45,114 --> 01:09:47,015
I don't think you'll need a jacket.

1768
01:09:47,550 --> 01:09:49,417
- You'll be sweating.
- Let's buy socks from there.

1769
01:09:49,418 --> 01:09:52,587
- Yeah, it's actually a little warm.
- You should be fine in short sleeves.

1770
01:09:52,588 --> 01:09:53,789
Totally.

1771
01:09:53,790 --> 01:09:56,058
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1772
01:09:56,059 --> 01:09:57,692
Yeah! Congratulations!

1773
01:09:57,693 --> 01:09:59,294
(Bye bye)

1774
01:09:59,300 --> 01:10:00,351
It suits you.

1775
01:10:00,352 --> 01:10:01,698
Let's go buy some socks.

1776
01:10:01,731 --> 01:10:03,762
There's a sock shop right in front of us.

1777
01:10:04,136 --> 01:10:05,968
I love this kind of thing.

1778
01:10:06,436 --> 01:10:07,704
This is fun.

1779
01:10:08,604 --> 01:10:10,673
- Do you have socks?
- Yes.

1780
01:10:12,816 --> 01:10:14,310
If you buy four, I'll give you a discount.

1781
01:10:14,311 --> 01:10:16,512
Really?

1782
01:10:16,878 --> 01:10:18,514
Then, how about 50?

1783
01:10:19,098 --> 01:10:20,650
How about 50?

1784
01:10:20,651 --> 01:10:21,484
Sixty.

1785
01:10:21,670 --> 01:10:22,518
Sixty?

1786
01:10:22,519 --> 01:10:26,522
You can do 50.

1787
01:10:27,690 --> 01:10:31,299
- You got this.
- You got this.

1788
01:10:31,858 --> 01:10:34,897
(The bargaining chorus makes
a long-awaited comeback.)

1789
01:10:35,037 --> 01:10:35,898
Fifty.

1790
01:10:35,899 --> 01:10:37,166
(Crying internally)

1791
01:10:37,177 --> 01:10:38,901
Fifty.

1792
01:10:40,336 --> 01:10:42,038
- Fifty?
- Okay.

1793
01:10:42,584 --> 01:10:44,464
(Deal sealed at 50,000 rupiah)

1794
01:10:45,408 --> 01:10:47,943
(Day 10: spent 200,000 rupiah
from the group funds)

1795
01:10:47,944 --> 01:10:50,046
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1796
01:10:51,013 --> 01:10:53,716
(It's much appreciated.)

1797
01:10:53,737 --> 01:10:54,644
We got everything.

1798
01:10:54,890 --> 01:10:56,185
- Done. Let's go home.
- Done!

1799
01:10:56,186 --> 01:10:58,087
- Let's go.
- Home is right in front of us.

1800
01:10:58,387 --> 01:11:02,558
Ramyeon would be amazing here.

1801
01:11:03,292 --> 01:11:04,829
They're so thick.

1802
01:11:04,830 --> 01:11:07,262
- Perfect for winter.
- I don't think my shoes are going to fit.

1803
01:11:07,310 --> 01:11:10,233
- I'll sleep with these on.
- They're warm the second you put them on.

1804
01:11:11,267 --> 01:11:12,935
It's so cute. It looks so good on you.

1805
01:11:13,088 --> 01:11:14,270
You chose so well.

1806
01:11:14,271 --> 01:11:15,104
This is crazy.

1807
01:11:15,105 --> 01:11:18,211
Everyone is so good
at picking things that suit each other.

1808
01:11:18,212 --> 01:11:19,884
We know each other's styles now.

1809
01:11:20,843 --> 01:11:22,843
Should we make ramyeon now?

1810
01:11:22,844 --> 01:11:23,679
Great.

1811
01:11:24,838 --> 01:11:26,282
(Getting ready to cook ramyeon together)

1812
01:11:26,283 --> 01:11:28,117
Do you put the seasoning in first
or the noodles?

1813
01:11:28,238 --> 01:11:30,520
- The seasoning, obviously.
- The seasoning.

1814
01:11:31,387 --> 01:11:33,189
We really are on the same wavelength.

1815
01:11:34,290 --> 01:11:36,526
- Of course the seasoning goes first.
- It's obvious.

1816
01:11:37,493 --> 01:11:39,195
Let's wait for the water to boil.

1817
01:11:40,659 --> 01:11:42,398
Which room do you want?

1818
01:11:42,399 --> 01:11:45,101
Should we play rock-paper-scissors
to make it fun?

1819
01:11:45,166 --> 01:11:46,402
Should we do that thing?

1820
01:11:47,370 --> 01:11:50,073
Sneak into the room you want to sleep in.

1821
01:11:51,007 --> 01:11:54,277
Everyone waits outside, then closes
the door and goes in one by one.

1822
01:11:54,313 --> 01:11:56,179
- You can stay right here.
- I see.

1823
01:11:56,180 --> 01:11:57,947
(Waiting in the bathroom)

1824
01:11:58,006 --> 01:12:00,683
If we all end up in the same room,

1825
01:12:00,833 --> 01:12:01,918
we can kick someone out.

1826
01:12:03,319 --> 01:12:05,459
That's hurtful. Why would you?

1827
01:12:05,460 --> 01:12:06,422
Kick someone out.

1828
01:12:06,621 --> 01:12:07,390
What do you think?

1829
01:12:07,391 --> 01:12:10,026
(Won Ji smells a chance for dopamine
and gets excited.)

1830
01:12:10,837 --> 01:12:12,862
Once you go in, close the door.

1831
01:12:13,462 --> 01:12:14,764
Okay, I love this.

1832
01:12:14,911 --> 01:12:16,499
Then once the door closes...

1833
01:12:16,604 --> 01:12:19,569
When you hear the door shut,
the next person can go.

1834
01:12:20,069 --> 01:12:22,904
- We'll be facing the other way.
- Okay.

1835
01:12:22,909 --> 01:12:23,540
(The game starts.)

1836
01:12:25,032 --> 01:12:27,352
(Sian goes first.)

1837
01:12:27,545 --> 01:12:28,744
The person...

1838
01:12:29,879 --> 01:12:31,714
I want to sleep with tonight is...

1839
01:12:32,014 --> 01:12:34,550
- It's "Single's Inferno."
- As expected.

1840
01:12:39,799 --> 01:12:42,419
(Sian can't make an easy choice.)

1841
01:12:42,485 --> 01:12:44,193
Sorry, but the water is boiling,
so please hurry up.

1842
01:12:44,194 --> 01:12:45,294
Okay, sorry.

1843
01:12:47,585 --> 01:12:50,019
(Pressed by Gabee, she makes her choice.)

1844
01:12:50,085 --> 01:12:52,972
(Sneaking in)

1845
01:12:53,332 --> 01:12:54,272
(Quietly enters the room)

1846
01:12:54,273 --> 01:12:55,571
We'll send the next person in.

1847
01:12:56,465 --> 01:12:58,718
Second up, Harimu. Let's go.

1848
01:12:58,758 --> 01:12:59,876
She already went?

1849
01:13:00,532 --> 01:13:02,545
She must have closed
the door really quietly.

1850
01:13:06,215 --> 01:13:09,619
I don't want to eat jjajangmyeon alone.

1851
01:13:09,919 --> 01:13:13,489
I don't want to eat jjajangmyeon alone.

1852
01:13:14,290 --> 01:13:16,521
(Then come in.)

1853
01:13:17,621 --> 01:13:22,827
(An empty room without Sian)

1854
01:13:23,833 --> 01:13:25,034
She closed the door.

1855
01:13:25,768 --> 01:13:27,270
I'm going.

1856
01:13:27,271 --> 01:13:28,859
(Won Ji goes third.)

1857
01:13:29,279 --> 01:13:31,974
(Jaws approaches.)

1858
01:13:32,885 --> 01:13:33,899
(Harimu, Sian)

1859
01:13:33,932 --> 01:13:35,244
Should I go here?

1860
01:13:35,578 --> 01:13:36,879
Or should I go here?

1861
01:13:37,798 --> 01:13:39,391
(Excitement up)

1862
01:13:39,431 --> 01:13:42,418
(Nerves up)

1863
01:13:42,751 --> 01:13:45,891
(Which will Won Ji choose?)

1864
01:13:46,011 --> 01:13:48,424
I'm going here.

1865
01:13:49,511 --> 01:13:52,345
(She chooses the room with Harimu.)

1866
01:13:55,179 --> 01:13:56,252
(Welcome.)

1867
01:13:58,445 --> 01:14:00,259
(A full-body welcome)

1868
01:14:00,312 --> 01:14:01,537
I'm going.

1869
01:14:01,538 --> 01:14:03,259
(Gabee goes last.)

1870
01:14:03,606 --> 01:14:05,606
Where is everyone?

1871
01:14:05,607 --> 01:14:07,944
I'm going with my first instinct.

1872
01:14:08,720 --> 01:14:11,113
I thought about choosing this room
from the very beginning.

1873
01:14:11,874 --> 01:14:14,174
(Sian, Gabee's eternal fan)

1874
01:14:14,900 --> 01:14:17,421
(Will Gabee's first instinct lead
her to Sian?)

1875
01:14:17,941 --> 01:14:20,281
(What will Gabee choose?)

1876
01:14:21,021 --> 01:14:23,395
(She chooses Won Ji and Harimu's room.)

1877
01:14:23,448 --> 01:14:24,160
Hello.

1878
01:14:24,261 --> 01:14:26,021
(Welcoming Scorpions)

1879
01:14:26,121 --> 01:14:28,197
What the heck?

1880
01:14:28,261 --> 01:14:30,428
(Calm down and take a look.)

1881
01:14:30,475 --> 01:14:31,400
What?

1882
01:14:31,401 --> 01:14:33,369
(A pair of scorpions
awaiting the spotlight)

1883
01:14:33,869 --> 01:14:35,204
Then the three of you can share.

1884
01:14:35,240 --> 01:14:37,273
(Pouting)

1885
01:14:37,540 --> 01:14:39,153
This is funny.

1886
01:14:39,154 --> 01:14:41,327
Three people can't share this room.

1887
01:14:41,373 --> 01:14:43,179
Then I'll pick from the three of you.

1888
01:14:43,180 --> 01:14:44,246
- Good idea.
- Good idea.

1889
01:14:44,327 --> 01:14:47,483
These are your beanies, right?

1890
01:14:47,750 --> 01:14:49,385
Should I close my eyes,

1891
01:14:49,425 --> 01:14:51,087
and put the hats on you?

1892
01:14:51,788 --> 01:14:55,891
Or you can turn around
while we mix them up and...

1893
01:14:56,125 --> 01:14:57,526
And I can pick one.

1894
01:14:57,827 --> 01:14:59,695
Then I'll close the door tight.

1895
01:15:00,595 --> 01:15:01,689
(Shutting)

1896
01:15:02,102 --> 01:15:04,649
(They're taking the game very seriously.)

1897
01:15:04,976 --> 01:15:06,335
(Shuffling)

1898
01:15:06,469 --> 01:15:07,336
(Mixing)

1899
01:15:07,783 --> 01:15:09,737
(Hats thoroughly mixed)

1900
01:15:09,837 --> 01:15:11,440
- Ready.
- Close your eyes.

1901
01:15:12,008 --> 01:15:14,076
Pick one from behind.

1902
01:15:14,208 --> 01:15:15,948
What does that even mean?

1903
01:15:15,949 --> 01:15:17,046
Seriously?

1904
01:15:17,375 --> 01:15:20,583
Numbers one, two, and three.

1905
01:15:20,941 --> 01:15:21,884
Hold on.

1906
01:15:21,885 --> 01:15:24,454
Does touching them make a difference?

1907
01:15:24,455 --> 01:15:25,841
(Why are they so serious?)

1908
01:15:26,088 --> 01:15:27,189
She's smelling it.

1909
01:15:27,190 --> 01:15:28,924
This one smells a little...

1910
01:15:28,957 --> 01:15:29,925
Like what?

1911
01:15:29,926 --> 01:15:30,950
(Sniffing)

1912
01:15:31,104 --> 01:15:32,557
This one smells the worst.

1913
01:15:33,264 --> 01:15:34,530
It really does.

1914
01:15:35,250 --> 01:15:38,534
I don't think I can share a room
with this person.

1915
01:15:39,570 --> 01:15:41,670
I'll go with the last one.

1916
01:15:44,006 --> 01:15:47,923
(Won Ji and Sian are
officially in the same room.)

1917
01:15:48,170 --> 01:15:50,813
This isn't what I smell like.

1918
01:15:51,180 --> 01:15:52,221
It smells.

1919
01:15:52,222 --> 01:15:53,082
(Sniffing)

1920
01:15:54,408 --> 01:15:55,701
This one doesn't smell.

1921
01:15:55,702 --> 01:15:57,119
This one really smells.

1922
01:15:57,120 --> 01:15:58,788
This one definitely smells the worst.

1923
01:15:59,334 --> 01:16:00,556
(Feeling wronged)

1924
01:16:00,557 --> 01:16:01,991
- You stink!
- This is so unfair.

1925
01:16:03,259 --> 01:16:07,063
(The room selection game ends.)

1926
01:16:07,180 --> 01:16:08,731
Let's see if the water is boiling.

1927
01:16:08,732 --> 01:16:10,799
A new partner, so it's even better, right?

1928
01:16:10,800 --> 01:16:11,885
Exactly.

1929
01:16:12,768 --> 01:16:14,343
(The water happens to be boiling.)

1930
01:16:15,203 --> 01:16:16,103
(Soup packet in)

1931
01:16:18,729 --> 01:16:19,616
(Noodles in)

1932
01:16:21,630 --> 01:16:25,622
(Waiting for the noodles to cook)

1933
01:16:25,915 --> 01:16:28,117
This looks delicious. Enjoy, everyone.

1934
01:16:28,118 --> 01:16:29,952
Let's eat.

1935
01:16:29,987 --> 01:16:31,447
I put in three packs.

1936
01:16:31,542 --> 01:16:34,390
- Cheers for noodles.
- Let's take a picture touching glasses.

1937
01:16:34,449 --> 01:16:35,925
- Cheers.
- It's so cute.

1938
01:16:36,325 --> 01:16:38,427
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

1939
01:16:38,428 --> 01:16:40,996
(Cup noodles at the final destination)

1940
01:16:41,849 --> 01:16:45,075
(Slurping down the ramyeon)

1941
01:16:45,515 --> 01:16:47,336
Gabee, you make great ramyeon.

1942
01:16:47,342 --> 01:16:48,804
- Right?
- Yes.

1943
01:16:49,638 --> 01:16:51,574
- What a relief.
- It's good.

1944
01:16:52,875 --> 01:16:55,678
Is there anything you packed
in your suitcase that you never used?

1945
01:16:55,813 --> 01:16:56,779
Anything you didn't use?

1946
01:16:56,800 --> 01:16:59,092
I already returned all that stuff.

1947
01:16:59,093 --> 01:17:00,432
Nothing.

1948
01:17:00,433 --> 01:17:01,150
Right?

1949
01:17:01,151 --> 01:17:03,220
I haven't worn my Oopsy tee.

1950
01:17:03,221 --> 01:17:05,221
You're wearing it tomorrow.

1951
01:17:06,260 --> 01:17:07,723
It's going to be so cold.

1952
01:17:07,990 --> 01:17:09,625
But I have to wear it.

1953
01:17:12,101 --> 01:17:15,668
(The late-night chat continues.)

1954
01:17:16,275 --> 01:17:21,639
(They reminisce
about the trip they've shared.)

1955
01:17:22,359 --> 01:17:27,113
(Lost in endless conversation,
they don't notice the time passing.)

1956
01:17:27,213 --> 01:17:29,311
- What time is it?
- It's 11 p.m.

1957
01:17:30,066 --> 01:17:31,580
We have to leave in four hours.

1958
01:17:31,646 --> 01:17:33,859
Oh, my goodness. No way!

1959
01:17:33,884 --> 01:17:36,018
Thanks for the meal.

1960
01:17:36,019 --> 01:17:37,783
(Cleaning up quickly for tomorrow)

1961
01:17:38,409 --> 01:17:41,023
(Time to go to sleep)

1962
01:17:41,803 --> 01:17:45,822
(Three hours until the sunrise tour)

1963
01:17:46,949 --> 01:17:51,382
(They quickly try to get some sleep.)

1964
01:17:56,306 --> 01:18:03,246
(Will they be able to safely finish
their final trip?)

1965
01:18:06,382 --> 01:18:09,051
(The sunrise squad heads out.)

1966
01:18:09,391 --> 01:18:11,831
(Climbing the dark mountain path)

1967
01:18:11,971 --> 01:18:12,831
In 10 minutes.

1968
01:18:13,031 --> 01:18:14,784
(The sun will rise in about 10 minutes.)

1969
01:18:14,891 --> 01:18:16,371
The sun is slowly rising.

1970
01:18:16,858 --> 01:18:19,351
(Following the slowly brightening dawn,)

1971
01:18:19,731 --> 01:18:22,344
(the four climb up the steep cliff.)

1972
01:18:22,723 --> 01:18:24,971
- In 30 seconds.
- Thirty seconds?

1973
01:18:28,424 --> 01:18:34,652
(Finally, an incredible sight unfolds
before their eyes.)

1974
01:18:34,985 --> 01:18:36,998
- This is unbelievable.
- I love this.

1975
01:18:37,598 --> 01:18:40,145
(A strange emotion fills them
as the sky turns red.)

1976
01:18:40,312 --> 01:18:42,092
Why do I feel like crying?

1977
01:18:42,392 --> 01:18:46,123
Don't cry, Sian. It's okay.

1978
01:18:46,616 --> 01:18:50,049
(They welcome
an unforgettable sunrise and...)

1979
01:18:50,403 --> 01:18:51,029
Guys.

1980
01:18:51,116 --> 01:18:52,996
(Are you ready to go to the volcano?)

1981
01:18:53,089 --> 01:18:54,689
Seriously?

1982
01:18:55,176 --> 01:18:56,749
(The final destination, Mount Bromo)

1983
01:18:57,176 --> 01:18:58,003
Bromo.

1984
01:18:58,563 --> 01:19:00,836
(Wait for us, Mount Bromo.)

1985
01:19:01,336 --> 01:19:04,095
(Racing across the endless plains,)

1986
01:19:04,608 --> 01:19:05,909
(crossing the sandy terrain,)

1987
01:19:06,189 --> 01:19:07,963
(and finally reaching the last obstacle)

1988
01:19:08,003 --> 01:19:10,049
- We're here.
- It's okay.

1989
01:19:10,329 --> 01:19:12,542
I can do it.

1990
01:19:13,235 --> 01:19:15,346
(Gabee's expression gradually hardens.)

1991
01:19:17,373 --> 01:19:19,400
- Wait.
- It's okay.

1992
01:19:19,953 --> 01:19:21,773
(Gabee suddenly stops walking.)

1993
01:19:22,086 --> 01:19:23,692
Should we go down together?

1994
01:19:24,503 --> 01:19:25,463
I'm going crazy.

1995
01:19:25,546 --> 01:19:27,246
Am I the only coward?

1996
01:19:27,606 --> 01:19:32,658
(The four stop
with the summit just ahead.)

1997
01:19:33,478 --> 01:19:36,531
(Will they be able to finish
their journey safely?)

1998
01:19:37,718 --> 01:19:42,131
I think I'm losing my mind.

1999
01:19:42,644 --> 01:19:45,289
(Sniffling)

2000
01:19:45,929 --> 01:19:47,835
We're going back to Korea now.

2001
01:19:48,395 --> 01:19:51,642
(It's already time to pack
for the final time.)

2002
01:19:52,582 --> 01:19:56,100
(Their final story awaits.)

2003
01:19:56,347 --> 01:19:57,607
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
